1
00:00:01,791 --> 00:00:03,875
Dear Uncle Napoleon, out of fear of the English,

2
00:00:03,916 --> 00:00:05,375
slept armed at night,

3
00:00:05,375 --> 00:00:08,250
and Agha Jan, day by day, fed his fantasies

4
00:00:08,375 --> 00:00:09,708
more and more.

5
00:00:10,666 --> 00:00:12,416
The war had still not shown

6
00:00:12,458 --> 00:00:14,583
its real effect on people's lives.

7
00:00:14,791 --> 00:00:16,208
It was only rumored that this year,

8
00:00:16,333 --> 00:00:17,583
the schools are closed,

9
00:00:17,625 --> 00:00:19,500
and provisions will become expensive and scarce.

10
00:00:20,291 --> 00:00:21,458
But our family

11
00:00:21,458 --> 00:00:24,000
still ate as well as before the war.

12
00:00:24,708 --> 00:00:26,833
Dear Uncle's terror of English policy

13
00:00:26,833 --> 00:00:27,875
only made them laugh,

14
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:31,000
and everyone was caught up in the matter of Qamar's pregnancy.

15
00:00:32,458 --> 00:00:34,416
When conscription was dissolved,

16
00:00:34,916 --> 00:00:35,958
my love for Leili

17
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:38,208
was in more danger than ever.

18
00:00:38,875 --> 00:00:40,666
Puri was coming back from the army,

19
00:00:41,125 --> 00:00:42,083
and Colonel Uncle

20
00:00:42,125 --> 00:00:43,833
had asked for Leili's hand.

21
00:00:44,458 --> 00:00:46,583
No one paid attention to my love.

22
00:00:47,083 --> 00:00:48,833
Everyone was thinking of saving Qamar,

23
00:00:48,833 --> 00:00:50,958
who was pregnant by an unknown man.

24
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:53,458
Lady Aziz-os-Saltaneh

25
00:00:53,666 --> 00:00:55,583
suspected Mr. Dust-Ali Khan,

26
00:00:55,875 --> 00:00:58,250
and Dear Uncle Napoleon, the English!

27
00:00:58,375 --> 00:01:00,375
(sound of horses trotting)

28
00:01:00,916 --> 00:01:05,875
Dear Uncle Napoleon Episode 10

29
00:01:06,833 --> 00:01:11,791
Based on the novel Dear Uncle Napoleon, written by Iraj Pezeshkzad

30
00:01:12,875 --> 00:01:14,875
Subtitle : Iman Soleimani Zadeh

31
00:01:19,375 --> 00:01:21,375
(sound of horses trotting)

32
00:01:30,125 --> 00:01:32,125
(sound of gunfire and the clamor of warriors)

33
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:16,000
♪ Ride of the valkyrie ♪

34
00:03:07,666 --> 00:03:09,291
Who would even believe it?

35
00:03:09,666 --> 00:03:11,291
Sir, you say something!

36
00:03:11,458 --> 00:03:12,958
But how is it possible!

37
00:03:14,750 --> 00:03:16,875
Tell the truth, or I swear I'll riddle you with bullets!

38
00:03:16,916 --> 00:03:18,041
Lady Aziz-os-Saltaneh!

39
00:03:18,375 --> 00:03:21,541
Watch out! That gun is loaded! Don't move!-

40
00:03:21,625 --> 00:03:22,625
Don't move!

41
00:03:22,916 --> 00:03:23,333
My dear Aziz!

42
00:03:23,333 --> 00:03:24,291
Stay where you are!

43
00:03:24,583 --> 00:03:26,541
Lady Aziz!

44
00:03:26,583 --> 00:03:29,166
By Leili's life, that gun is loaded!

45
00:03:29,250 --> 00:03:30,458
I put a cartridge in it,

46
00:03:30,458 --> 00:03:32,000
so if the English army arrives,

47
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:33,083
we won't be caught off guard!

48
00:03:33,125 --> 00:03:33,875
You people, step aside!

49
00:03:33,958 --> 00:03:35,708
All of you sit in your places, shut up!

50
00:03:35,750 --> 00:03:36,583
My dear Aziz!

51
00:03:36,708 --> 00:03:37,000
Me?!

52
00:03:37,208 --> 00:03:38,916
Shameless coward!

53
00:03:39,166 --> 00:03:41,000
Say it! Say it, you coward!

54
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:43,416
Why did you tell Qamar to say it was Allahverdi's doing? Say it!

55
00:03:43,541 --> 00:03:44,208
Say it!

56
00:03:44,291 --> 00:03:45,166
By God!

57
00:03:45,208 --> 00:03:46,916
By my mother's soul, I didn't say it!

58
00:03:46,958 --> 00:03:48,875
And if I did, I meant no harm! Lady Aziz!-

59
00:03:48,916 --> 00:03:50,875
I just wanted to avoid a scandal!

60
00:03:51,166 --> 00:03:52,625
Don't waste the bullet on him! My dear Aziz!-

61
00:03:52,833 --> 00:03:53,666
Give me the gun!

62
00:03:53,750 --> 00:03:55,916
Dear Aziz... give it... let go... give it to me!

63
00:03:55,916 --> 00:03:56,833
Let go of me, Asdollah!

64
00:03:56,875 --> 00:03:57,250
Run!

65
00:03:58,666 --> 00:03:59,500
Go on, go!

66
00:03:59,541 --> 00:04:01,625
While she's busy, run! Go!

67
00:04:01,916 --> 00:04:02,958
The gun! Eh, eh, eh!

68
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:03,958
Saint Abbas, help!-

69
00:04:03,958 --> 00:04:04,666
Stop, you coward!

70
00:04:04,666 --> 00:04:05,791
Stop! Hold him!-

71
00:04:05,833 --> 00:04:07,125
(sound of the telephone ringing)

72
00:04:07,166 --> 00:04:08,416
Asdollah! Hold him! Grab him!

73
00:04:08,458 --> 00:04:09,041
Yes? Asdollah!-

74
00:04:09,083 --> 00:04:09,791
I'll cut you to pieces!

75
00:04:09,833 --> 00:04:11,250
They want you! I'm not here! Say I'm not!-

76
00:04:11,291 --> 00:04:11,958
He says he's not here!

77
00:04:11,958 --> 00:04:13,000
(clamor of the gathering)

78
00:04:13,041 --> 00:04:14,791
Don't hit! For God's sake, don't hit!

79
00:04:14,833 --> 00:04:15,708
Don't hit!

80
00:04:15,750 --> 00:04:16,583
(sound of a gunshot)

81
00:04:16,916 --> 00:04:19,500
(sound of Dust-Ali's scream and the clamor of the gathering)

82
00:04:22,458 --> 00:04:23,333
Blood!

83
00:04:23,333 --> 00:04:24,125
Dust-Ali!

84
00:04:24,166 --> 00:04:24,958
Dust-Ali!

85
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:26,333
Dust-Ali, what happened?!

86
00:04:26,375 --> 00:04:27,708
Come, help!

87
00:04:27,750 --> 00:04:28,666
Where did it hit?

88
00:04:28,708 --> 00:04:29,416
Dust-Ali!

89
00:04:30,833 --> 00:04:33,208
Woman, look what you've done!

90
00:04:33,250 --> 00:04:34,291
Where did it hit you? Blood!-

91
00:04:34,333 --> 00:04:35,875
Where did it hit you? It's burning!-

92
00:04:35,916 --> 00:04:36,916
Mama, Mama!

93
00:04:36,916 --> 00:04:38,250
Did you kill him or not?

94
00:04:38,250 --> 00:04:40,583
Good job, Mama!

95
00:04:41,041 --> 00:04:43,041
Mama dear! You did a very good thing,

96
00:04:43,083 --> 00:04:44,500
you killed Dad Dust-Ali!

97
00:04:44,916 --> 00:04:48,208
Remember he kept saying go to the doctor and get rid of your baby?

98
00:04:48,208 --> 00:04:49,000
Eh! Let go, girl!

99
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:50,125
Serves him right!

100
00:04:50,166 --> 00:04:53,416
Now he can't kill my baby anymore, right?

101
00:04:54,166 --> 00:04:55,083
Dust-Ali!

102
00:04:55,083 --> 00:04:55,625
Dust-Ali!

103
00:04:55,666 --> 00:04:56,916
At least let me see what happened!

104
00:04:56,916 --> 00:04:57,583
Blood!

105
00:04:57,791 --> 00:04:59,791
(Dust-Ali screams)

106
00:04:59,833 --> 00:05:00,500
Don't be afraid!-

107
00:05:01,375 --> 00:05:02,416
All right!

108
00:05:02,416 --> 00:05:03,625
All right!

109
00:05:04,833 --> 00:05:05,541
Let me see what happened!

110
00:05:05,541 --> 00:05:06,208
I'm dying, Doctor!

111
00:05:06,208 --> 00:05:08,750
Let me see where it hit you, man!

112
00:05:08,791 --> 00:05:10,458
My bum, my bum!

113
00:05:10,500 --> 00:05:12,250
Oh, oh! Where did it hit?-

114
00:05:12,250 --> 00:05:13,083
No sir!

115
00:05:13,083 --> 00:05:15,000
This was a blister, now it burst!

116
00:05:15,041 --> 00:05:18,250
Asdollah, shame on you! Enough joking!

117
00:05:18,500 --> 00:05:19,416
Moment!

118
00:05:19,458 --> 00:05:21,750
He'll never sit on that seat again!

119
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:23,416
(Dust-Ali moans)

120
00:05:23,416 --> 00:05:24,958
Don't move, it will get worse!

121
00:05:24,958 --> 00:05:27,208
Agha Joon, Agha Joon! What happened? What happened?

122
00:05:27,208 --> 00:05:27,875
It's nothing!

123
00:05:28,625 --> 00:05:30,375
I'm dying!

124
00:05:30,875 --> 00:05:32,083
Uncle Asdollah, what happened?

125
00:05:32,333 --> 00:05:32,916
Huh?

126
00:05:32,916 --> 00:05:33,708
What happened?

127
00:05:33,708 --> 00:05:34,416
Nothing!

128
00:05:34,416 --> 00:05:36,875
The poor devil, for one trip to San Francisco,

129
00:05:36,916 --> 00:05:38,958
now has to sleep face-down for the rest of his life!

130
00:05:38,958 --> 00:05:39,625
But why?

131
00:05:39,625 --> 00:05:40,958
His dear Aziz shot him with a bullet!

132
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:41,833
Lady Aziz?!

133
00:05:42,541 --> 00:05:44,000
Let me see, man! Let me see!

134
00:05:44,041 --> 00:05:45,166
Ay, ay, ay, ay!

135
00:05:45,916 --> 00:05:48,041
It's badly torn up!

136
00:05:48,083 --> 00:05:49,625
Moment! Moment!

137
00:05:49,875 --> 00:05:51,333
He's fooling you!

138
00:05:51,333 --> 00:05:52,333
Nothing's happened to him!

139
00:05:52,750 --> 00:05:53,666
Two little pellets,

140
00:05:53,666 --> 00:05:55,916
that could barely lame a partridge's leg,

141
00:05:56,333 --> 00:05:58,250
against a ton of that donkey Dust-Ali's backside,

142
00:05:58,291 --> 00:05:59,416
what can they do?

143
00:06:00,666 --> 00:06:01,708
He's so scared of Lady Aziz,

144
00:06:01,708 --> 00:06:02,875
he's playing dead!

145
00:06:02,916 --> 00:06:03,416
Asdollah!-

146
00:06:04,208 --> 00:06:05,750
Stop it, Asdollah!

147
00:06:05,750 --> 00:06:07,458
This poor man is dying!

148
00:06:07,458 --> 00:06:08,333
Instead of talking,

149
00:06:08,375 --> 00:06:11,666
come help us get him to Dr. Naser-ol-Hokama's house!

150
00:06:11,916 --> 00:06:13,833
Dr. Naser-ol-Hokama is no use at all!

151
00:06:13,833 --> 00:06:15,791
We have to get him to the hospital!

152
00:06:15,833 --> 00:06:17,583
The Colonel is right! The hospital is better!

153
00:06:17,625 --> 00:06:18,791
No, no!

154
00:06:18,833 --> 00:06:20,208
I don't think that's wise!

155
00:06:20,250 --> 00:06:22,000
Think of something else for him!

156
00:06:22,291 --> 00:06:24,291
Forget the hospital!

157
00:06:24,458 --> 00:06:26,750
It'll turn into a big affair!

158
00:06:26,791 --> 00:06:28,750
The family's honor is at stake!

159
00:06:28,750 --> 00:06:30,625
You are killing him with your own hands!

160
00:06:30,666 --> 00:06:32,416
Let's rush him to another hospital then!

161
00:06:32,458 --> 00:06:34,833
Please, don't interfere anymore!

162
00:06:34,833 --> 00:06:36,500
You're being unreasonable, Sir!

163
00:06:36,541 --> 00:06:37,291
Dust-Ali!

164
00:06:37,291 --> 00:06:39,625
Sir, let us take him to some hospital! Take me somewhere!-

165
00:06:39,666 --> 00:06:41,833
There's no need for you to interfere!

166
00:06:41,875 --> 00:06:43,166
I have no say in this!

167
00:06:44,666 --> 00:06:45,375
Doctor dear!

168
00:06:45,458 --> 00:06:47,458
Mr. Doctor! Where are you going?

169
00:06:47,500 --> 00:06:48,916
It has nothing to do with me!

170
00:06:48,958 --> 00:06:49,833
Mr. Doctor!

171
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:51,583
Now you're acting like a child too!

172
00:06:51,958 --> 00:06:53,416
Don't be afraid, Dust-Ali, don't be afraid!

173
00:06:54,583 --> 00:06:56,083
Don't be afraid, Lady Aziz.

174
00:06:56,208 --> 00:06:58,916
Nothing will happen to him! God take me!-

175
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:03,458
If he dies, what will become of me! It was an accident! Don't be upset!-

176
00:07:03,458 --> 00:07:05,500
Poor unlucky me.

177
00:07:05,500 --> 00:07:07,125
Come to my rescue...-

178
00:07:07,583 --> 00:07:08,625
Mr. Doctor!

179
00:07:08,625 --> 00:07:11,583
For the sake of friendship and neighborliness!

180
00:07:12,041 --> 00:07:12,833
Mash Ghasem!

181
00:07:12,875 --> 00:07:13,750
Yes, Mr. Doctor?

182
00:07:13,791 --> 00:07:15,583
Didn't you say that

183
00:07:15,666 --> 00:07:17,500
his leg was wounded?

184
00:07:17,541 --> 00:07:19,666
Honestly, Mr. Doctor, from where we saw it,

185
00:07:19,708 --> 00:07:21,416
we thought it was the top of his leg!

186
00:07:22,375 --> 00:07:24,500
That one has been hit by a bullet!

187
00:07:24,625 --> 00:07:26,041
He's been shot!

188
00:07:26,166 --> 00:07:28,583
I am not a surgeon!

189
00:07:28,583 --> 00:07:30,875
You have to take him to the hospital!

190
00:07:31,208 --> 00:07:33,000
Mr. Doctor!

191
00:07:33,833 --> 00:07:36,333
For the sake of friendship!

192
00:07:36,708 --> 00:07:38,708
For the sake of kinship!

193
00:07:38,916 --> 00:07:42,291
For the sake of neighborliness I beg you,

194
00:07:42,291 --> 00:07:44,416
treat Dust-Ali!

195
00:07:44,416 --> 00:07:46,125
An accident has happened!

196
00:07:46,166 --> 00:07:47,291
Please,

197
00:07:47,333 --> 00:07:49,416
whatever is in your power,

198
00:07:49,416 --> 00:07:51,083
even if it's for his wife's sake,

199
00:07:51,083 --> 00:07:52,416
spare no effort.

200
00:07:52,416 --> 00:07:55,666
I cannot take him to the hospital!

201
00:07:55,916 --> 00:07:57,083
There's a matter

202
00:07:57,125 --> 00:08:00,541
that I'll explain to you in detail later.

203
00:08:00,583 --> 00:08:03,291
Then it's your responsibility!

204
00:08:03,541 --> 00:08:06,208
If, God forbid,

205
00:08:06,958 --> 00:08:08,750
it festers,

206
00:08:08,833 --> 00:08:10,833
then I am not responsible!

207
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:12,000
I accept.

208
00:08:12,791 --> 00:08:13,666
I accept.

209
00:08:13,916 --> 00:08:16,166
The gentlemen must all go.

210
00:08:16,666 --> 00:08:20,166
With all this crowd, I cannot treat him.

211
00:08:21,750 --> 00:08:23,250
I must stay.

212
00:08:23,625 --> 00:08:26,125
Poor broken-hearted, wretched me,

213
00:08:26,166 --> 00:08:29,708
must stay and see what disaster befalls me.

214
00:08:30,750 --> 00:08:33,750
Thank you, Lady Aziz!

215
00:08:33,916 --> 00:08:36,500
You too must kindly go outside!

216
00:08:36,833 --> 00:08:40,000
Honestly, I won't lay a hand on the patient.

217
00:08:44,333 --> 00:08:46,000
But my assistant isn't here.

218
00:08:46,041 --> 00:08:48,291
Just one of you stay to help me.

219
00:08:48,333 --> 00:08:49,208
Gladly.

220
00:08:49,416 --> 00:08:51,875
We know a great deal about this sort of thing.

221
00:08:52,250 --> 00:08:54,541
Why lie? The grave is this close!

222
00:08:55,208 --> 00:08:57,625
Once we had a fellow townsman

223
00:08:57,666 --> 00:08:59,916
who'd been knifed in the spleen!

224
00:08:59,958 --> 00:09:01,875
And with our own hands, we...

225
00:09:01,916 --> 00:09:05,625
All right, all right! Thank you! Thank you!

226
00:09:05,666 --> 00:09:07,291
You go too, Mash Ghasem.

227
00:09:07,375 --> 00:09:08,791
No need for you to stay!

228
00:09:08,833 --> 00:09:09,500
At your service, at your service!

229
00:09:09,500 --> 00:09:11,416
You talk an awful lot.

230
00:09:13,333 --> 00:09:14,416
You, please.

231
00:09:14,541 --> 00:09:15,208
Please!

232
00:09:15,250 --> 00:09:15,750
At your service!

233
00:09:20,541 --> 00:09:21,750
Now then, Saeed!

234
00:09:22,125 --> 00:09:23,125
You,

235
00:09:23,166 --> 00:09:25,166
you're not afraid of blood, are you? Huh?

236
00:09:25,166 --> 00:09:26,041
Me, Mr. Doctor?

237
00:09:26,083 --> 00:09:27,750
No! Rest assured!

238
00:09:27,958 --> 00:09:30,416
Good for you, my boy.

239
00:09:33,083 --> 00:09:34,500
Step aside!

240
00:09:35,625 --> 00:09:36,541
What did you say, Mr. Doctor?

241
00:09:36,583 --> 00:09:37,500
Goodbye!

242
00:09:37,500 --> 00:09:39,458
I said get out of here! Yes, yes, yes!-

243
00:09:39,541 --> 00:09:41,333
Mr. Doctor said goodbye!

244
00:09:41,333 --> 00:09:43,458
Then help me take his clothes off.

245
00:09:44,083 --> 00:09:46,875
(Dust-Ali moans)

246
00:10:07,250 --> 00:10:08,208
Dust-Ali!

247
00:10:09,875 --> 00:10:10,750
Dust-Ali!

248
00:10:11,583 --> 00:10:13,083
Can you heer me?

249
00:10:30,666 --> 00:10:31,916
(Dust-Ali shouts)

250
00:10:33,083 --> 00:10:34,708
My wife! My wife! Is my wife here?

251
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:35,541
Huh?

252
00:10:35,916 --> 00:10:37,500
No one is here.

253
00:10:37,583 --> 00:10:39,875
Only I and this boy are here.

254
00:10:40,041 --> 00:10:41,458
It's killing me!

255
00:10:41,583 --> 00:10:43,125
What happened? Where did it hit?

256
00:10:43,500 --> 00:10:45,458
Relax!

257
00:10:45,500 --> 00:10:47,375
It's nothing important!

258
00:10:47,500 --> 00:10:50,000
Three small pellets

259
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:51,833
in his butt!

260
00:10:51,916 --> 00:10:53,791
And from a good distance, too!

261
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:56,291
They haven't gone in deep!

262
00:10:56,333 --> 00:10:58,833
Can you bear me taking them out?

263
00:10:58,875 --> 00:11:00,791
Or shall I send you to the hospital?

264
00:11:00,833 --> 00:11:01,875
I can bear it!

265
00:11:01,875 --> 00:11:03,000
I can bear it!

266
00:11:03,000 --> 00:11:03,916
I can bear it,

267
00:11:03,958 --> 00:11:06,291
I've been in pain for over an hour

268
00:11:06,333 --> 00:11:07,916
without making a sound!

269
00:11:08,125 --> 00:11:10,083
Why didn't you moan?!

270
00:11:10,875 --> 00:11:12,416
Out of fear of that hag!

271
00:11:12,625 --> 00:11:14,333
Out of fear of that murderer!

272
00:11:14,708 --> 00:11:16,791
If she finds out I'm not badly hurt,

273
00:11:16,916 --> 00:11:18,916
she'll kill me by morning!

274
00:11:19,250 --> 00:11:20,916
She'll strangle me!

275
00:11:21,833 --> 00:11:24,875
I don't have anesthesia equipment here!

276
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:27,291
You have to be able to bear it,

277
00:11:27,500 --> 00:11:29,166
while I, with forceps,

278
00:11:29,333 --> 00:11:30,916
take the pellets out.

279
00:11:31,083 --> 00:11:32,041
Can you endure?

280
00:11:32,041 --> 00:11:34,208
I can endure! Bless you, dear Doctor!

281
00:11:34,833 --> 00:11:35,708
Bless you!

282
00:11:35,875 --> 00:11:36,791
Bless you!

283
00:11:36,875 --> 00:11:38,458
Only if you tell my wife

284
00:11:38,625 --> 00:11:40,291
his condition is very grave!

285
00:11:40,500 --> 00:11:43,500
There's no hope he'll survive!

286
00:11:44,166 --> 00:11:46,583
This is the second time, Dust-Ali!

287
00:11:46,666 --> 00:11:49,666
She once tried to cut off your manhood,

288
00:11:49,958 --> 00:11:53,250
this time you dodged the bullet!

289
00:11:53,500 --> 00:11:58,458
Watch out! The third time, you're done for!

290
00:11:58,458 --> 00:12:00,083
I know, I know, Mr. Doctor!

291
00:12:00,583 --> 00:12:03,708
One more time, and I'm finished! I know!

292
00:12:04,125 --> 00:12:05,458
Scream!

293
00:12:05,750 --> 00:12:08,291
I'm going to open the door

294
00:12:08,333 --> 00:12:09,625
and bring the forceps!

295
00:12:09,666 --> 00:12:10,333
All right!

296
00:12:10,333 --> 00:12:15,375
(Dust-Ali starts screaming)

297
00:12:15,458 --> 00:12:17,291
Doctor, how's he doing?

298
00:12:17,541 --> 00:12:20,625
Take Lady Aziz home, quickly.

299
00:12:23,125 --> 00:12:25,583
Dust-Ali's condition is very bad!

300
00:12:26,333 --> 00:12:27,375
Mr. Doctor!

301
00:12:27,375 --> 00:12:29,833
Did the bullet hit a dangerous place?

302
00:12:29,958 --> 00:12:32,166
I'm doing everything I can.

303
00:12:32,750 --> 00:12:34,750
(Aziz-os-Saltaneh cries)

304
00:12:44,375 --> 00:12:45,000
Doctor!

305
00:12:45,416 --> 00:12:47,166
Tell me, how's he doing?

306
00:12:47,208 --> 00:12:49,458
Tell me, what disaster has struck me?

307
00:12:50,083 --> 00:12:53,333
Be strong, Madam!

308
00:12:53,500 --> 00:12:55,958
For now I can't say anything!

309
00:12:56,833 --> 00:13:00,250
It depends on his body's resistance.

310
00:13:01,541 --> 00:13:02,708
If he makes it

311
00:13:02,791 --> 00:13:04,750
through the night...

312
00:13:04,791 --> 00:13:07,291
maybe he'll stay alive! Don't cry, Lady Aziz!-

313
00:13:07,333 --> 00:13:08,791
Surely he'll get well!

314
00:13:08,791 --> 00:13:11,000
He's fine, don't cry! Yes!-

315
00:13:11,000 --> 00:13:12,250
Lady Aziz?

316
00:13:12,541 --> 00:13:15,541
Tonight let him stay at Sir's house,

317
00:13:15,750 --> 00:13:17,375
which is closer to me.

318
00:13:17,750 --> 00:13:20,500
For now I've given him morphine,

319
00:13:20,666 --> 00:13:22,416
so that if he comes to,

320
00:13:22,875 --> 00:13:24,666
he won't be in too much pain!

321
00:13:25,166 --> 00:13:26,666
Good night!

322
00:13:26,708 --> 00:13:28,500
Moment! Moment!

323
00:13:30,583 --> 00:13:31,375
Duki!

324
00:13:31,375 --> 00:13:34,708
Tell me the truth! Is Dust-Ali in a bad way?

325
00:13:34,791 --> 00:13:36,000
When a grown man

326
00:13:36,083 --> 00:13:38,166
plays dead like this,

327
00:13:38,208 --> 00:13:40,583
it must be out of fear of his wife!

328
00:13:41,083 --> 00:13:42,708
Good night!

329
00:13:42,833 --> 00:13:44,500
Moment!

330
00:13:45,791 --> 00:13:47,500
You know him!

331
00:13:47,541 --> 00:13:48,916
Rest assured!

332
00:13:48,958 --> 00:13:50,791
I won't say a word to anyone!

333
00:13:51,250 --> 00:13:53,458
Are you ready, Mr. Dust-Ali Khan?

334
00:13:53,500 --> 00:13:54,541
A drop of water!

335
00:13:54,583 --> 00:13:56,375
A drop of water! All right!-

336
00:13:56,708 --> 00:13:57,500
I'm thirsty!

337
00:13:57,666 --> 00:14:00,166
Stop all this wailing!

338
00:14:00,166 --> 00:14:01,291
Lie on your stomach.

339
00:14:01,291 --> 00:14:01,875
I'm thirsty.

340
00:14:01,875 --> 00:14:04,041
I don't have any anesthetic.

341
00:14:04,083 --> 00:14:05,458
You have to bear it!

342
00:14:05,458 --> 00:14:06,125
At your service!

343
00:14:15,875 --> 00:14:17,125
Ready?

344
00:14:17,291 --> 00:14:18,958
Yes, Mr. Doctor! I'm ready!

345
00:14:19,541 --> 00:14:20,666
I'm ready!

346
00:14:21,875 --> 00:14:23,125
I'm ready....

347
00:14:23,166 --> 00:14:24,166
(Dust-Ali shouts)

348
00:14:24,166 --> 00:14:25,875
Well done!

349
00:14:42,083 --> 00:14:44,083
(Dust-Ali bellows)

350
00:14:50,416 --> 00:14:51,541
Salaam alaykom, Sir!

351
00:14:51,750 --> 00:14:52,500
Salaam alaykom!

352
00:14:54,250 --> 00:14:54,666
What happened?

353
00:14:55,041 --> 00:14:56,541
Madam, why cry kartahe?

354
00:14:56,583 --> 00:14:57,458
What happened?

355
00:14:58,666 --> 00:15:01,041
I, in sleep, heard the sound of a bullet!

356
00:15:01,083 --> 00:15:03,541
I came and said perhaps help kartahe!

357
00:15:03,708 --> 00:15:05,041
Mahatma Gandhi said:

358
00:15:05,041 --> 00:15:07,541
Neighbor with neighbor must help kartahe!

359
00:15:07,583 --> 00:15:10,083
I many wars fight kartahe!

360
00:15:10,416 --> 00:15:12,000
Tataq! Taq taq, tataq!

361
00:15:12,000 --> 00:15:13,791
I know the sound of a bullet!

362
00:15:13,791 --> 00:15:14,333
Very good!

363
00:15:23,333 --> 00:15:24,250
Mr., Mr.... Mr. Doctor!

364
00:15:24,291 --> 00:15:25,875
Surgery no use kartahe,

365
00:15:25,916 --> 00:15:26,875
never! never!

366
00:15:26,916 --> 00:15:28,125
For these wounds,

367
00:15:28,666 --> 00:15:31,250
I have a special oil. Genuine Indian!

368
00:15:31,541 --> 00:15:33,291
At once the wound heal kartahe!

369
00:15:33,416 --> 00:15:34,541
I go bring, at once!

370
00:15:34,541 --> 00:15:35,250
Very good!

371
00:15:35,333 --> 00:15:36,750
For healing, good! Good!

372
00:15:37,416 --> 00:15:39,708
Ghasem! Close the door!

373
00:15:39,708 --> 00:15:40,500
Run, close it!

374
00:15:40,500 --> 00:15:40,916
At your service!

375
00:15:40,958 --> 00:15:42,791
Hurry! Close the door!

376
00:15:43,416 --> 00:15:44,166
Don't you dare

377
00:15:44,208 --> 00:15:48,125
open the door to this unpatriotic good-for-nothing!

378
00:15:48,458 --> 00:15:50,625
If this Indian loved his country,

379
00:15:50,625 --> 00:15:52,541
wouldn't be serving Churchill!

380
00:15:52,708 --> 00:15:56,291
This spy has pulled every trick he knows!

381
00:15:56,500 --> 00:15:59,625
Now that they've seen their plot won't work,

382
00:15:59,916 --> 00:16:02,333
they've decided to kill Dust-Ali!

383
00:16:02,333 --> 00:16:06,208
He's gone to bring Indian oil, to kill Dust-Ali!

384
00:16:07,541 --> 00:16:09,333
Why does he want to kill Mr. Dust-Ali Khan?!

385
00:16:09,500 --> 00:16:11,500
But Dust-Ali too

386
00:16:11,541 --> 00:16:13,875
was going to reveal some secrets

387
00:16:13,916 --> 00:16:15,291
of the English plot... (Dust-Ali shouts)

388
00:16:15,458 --> 00:16:16,541
to me!

389
00:16:16,583 --> 00:16:17,541
Don't cry, my dear!

390
00:16:17,583 --> 00:16:18,291
Don't cry!

391
00:16:18,291 --> 00:16:19,000
Be calm!

392
00:16:19,250 --> 00:16:19,833
Be calm!

393
00:16:19,833 --> 00:16:20,750
Sir, even if this wretch

394
00:16:20,791 --> 00:16:22,208
stands here till tomorrow morning,

395
00:16:22,250 --> 00:16:23,416
we won't open the door to him!

396
00:16:23,583 --> 00:16:25,583
We know what that oil of his is!

397
00:16:25,625 --> 00:16:27,250
It's a black-colored oil

398
00:16:27,250 --> 00:16:28,833
that they take from a viper's liver!

399
00:16:29,250 --> 00:16:31,208
Hold its tin under an elephant's nose,

400
00:16:31,458 --> 00:16:34,166
and it goes up in smoke! (Dust-Ali shouts)

401
00:16:34,208 --> 00:16:35,083
Oh no!

402
00:16:35,125 --> 00:16:35,958
Aww!

403
00:16:36,708 --> 00:16:37,333
Aww!

404
00:16:37,833 --> 00:16:39,458
Oh, God take me!

405
00:16:39,541 --> 00:16:40,791
Easy! Oh, woe is me!

406
00:16:40,791 --> 00:16:41,791
Don't let me fall! Easy with him!-

407
00:16:41,833 --> 00:16:42,916
Don't let him fall down!

408
00:16:42,958 --> 00:16:44,083
Oh, dear God!

409
00:16:44,166 --> 00:16:45,500
Oh, good Lord! Hold him higher, Mash Ghasem!-

410
00:16:45,791 --> 00:16:46,958
How heavy he is!

411
00:16:47,000 --> 00:16:48,708
Hold his head higher! I'm a wreck!-

412
00:16:48,708 --> 00:16:51,041
Don't let his head bump! Don't drop me, I'll be crushed!-

413
00:16:51,291 --> 00:16:52,208
Careful, for God's sake! Relax-

414
00:16:52,208 --> 00:16:52,833
What happened, Agha Jan?

415
00:16:52,875 --> 00:16:53,708
Easy!

416
00:16:53,708 --> 00:16:54,666
Step aside, man!

417
00:16:54,666 --> 00:16:58,416
(clamor of the gathering)

418
00:16:58,458 --> 00:16:59,666
He's made a mess for us!

419
00:16:59,666 --> 00:17:00,958
What kind of farce is this?

420
00:17:01,208 --> 00:17:01,833
Look!

421
00:17:02,583 --> 00:17:03,958
Watch out, Mash Ghasem!

422
00:17:04,875 --> 00:17:05,541
Step aside!

423
00:17:09,500 --> 00:17:11,375
Step aside, open the way!

424
00:17:11,708 --> 00:17:14,125
(clamor of the gathering)

425
00:17:14,416 --> 00:17:15,500
They've brought him from the hospital!-

426
00:17:18,375 --> 00:17:19,291
Watch out!

427
00:17:21,208 --> 00:17:22,208
Step aside!

428
00:17:24,916 --> 00:17:25,916
Clear the area, let's see!

429
00:17:25,916 --> 00:17:26,833
Go about your business!

430
00:17:26,875 --> 00:17:28,416
Go on! Didn't you hear them? Go already!

431
00:17:28,458 --> 00:17:29,166
Go already!

432
00:17:29,750 --> 00:17:32,125
Salaam alaykom, Sir! How is your patient?

433
00:17:32,166 --> 00:17:32,916
Thank God!

434
00:17:32,916 --> 00:17:34,083
He's much better!

435
00:17:34,125 --> 00:17:38,125
Thank you very much for keeping people from bothering him!

436
00:17:38,166 --> 00:17:39,500
You may go now.

437
00:17:39,500 --> 00:17:41,500
But Sir, we have a duty to report!

438
00:17:41,500 --> 00:17:42,916
After all, someone has been shot!

439
00:17:44,125 --> 00:17:45,166
At your service! Please.

440
00:17:50,916 --> 00:17:51,708
Agha Joon!

441
00:17:51,750 --> 00:17:53,875
It wasn't on purpose!

442
00:17:54,083 --> 00:17:56,500
It was an accident, my dear!

443
00:17:56,791 --> 00:17:59,125
He was cleaning the gun,

444
00:17:59,125 --> 00:18:00,166
it went off!

445
00:18:00,416 --> 00:18:01,000
Well...

446
00:18:01,125 --> 00:18:03,083
Thank God he's doing well now,

447
00:18:03,125 --> 00:18:05,166
and no one has complained!

448
00:18:05,416 --> 00:18:06,666
Oh, come now, Sir!

449
00:18:06,708 --> 00:18:08,166
How was he cleaning the gun,

450
00:18:08,166 --> 00:18:09,500
that the bullet hit his butt!

451
00:18:09,500 --> 00:18:11,375
You think we're donkeys, no offense?

452
00:18:12,250 --> 00:18:12,958
Azizollah Khan!

453
00:18:13,000 --> 00:18:14,500
How you nitpick!

454
00:18:14,958 --> 00:18:17,791
The poor man was playing with the gun,

455
00:18:17,833 --> 00:18:19,166
and it went off, that's all!

456
00:18:19,208 --> 00:18:19,958
Ghasem! Eh! It went off!-

457
00:18:20,875 --> 00:18:23,416
Give him something yourself and send him off!

458
00:18:23,458 --> 00:18:24,208
At your service, at your service!

459
00:18:24,250 --> 00:18:24,708
Yes?

460
00:18:24,708 --> 00:18:27,500
Goodness, you've been a policeman for 10, 15 years.

461
00:18:27,541 --> 00:18:28,000
Aha!

462
00:18:28,041 --> 00:18:28,791
It's a bullet, after all!

463
00:18:28,833 --> 00:18:30,208
Sometimes it hits a person's eye,

464
00:18:30,208 --> 00:18:31,416
sometimes a person's liver,

465
00:18:31,458 --> 00:18:32,833
sometimes it hits there!

466
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:33,625
Yes!

467
00:18:33,666 --> 00:18:35,291
We had a fellow townsman

468
00:18:35,333 --> 00:18:37,500
who once had a bullet hit his belly...

469
00:18:43,125 --> 00:18:44,666
(Leili cries)

470
00:18:44,708 --> 00:18:45,333
Leili dear!

471
00:18:45,333 --> 00:18:45,791
Come.

472
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:48,041
Don't cry so much!

473
00:18:48,875 --> 00:18:49,791
Did you read my letter?

474
00:18:49,833 --> 00:18:51,625
But Dust-Ali is dying!

475
00:18:52,291 --> 00:18:53,000
Dustali?!

476
00:18:53,000 --> 00:18:54,750
Why did you write that I should tear up the letter?

477
00:18:54,791 --> 00:18:56,041
Nothing's happened to Dust-Ali Khan!

478
00:18:56,625 --> 00:18:58,500
Don't let my letter fall into Dear Uncle's hands!

479
00:18:58,708 --> 00:19:01,166
He's moaning like that out of fear of Lady Aziz!

480
00:19:02,291 --> 00:19:02,833
Go, go!

481
00:19:02,875 --> 00:19:04,125
Go, I heard the door!

482
00:19:11,875 --> 00:19:13,416
(Aziz-os-Saltaneh cries)

483
00:19:13,500 --> 00:19:14,541
What can I say...

484
00:19:22,958 --> 00:19:24,958
(Dust-Ali moans)

485
00:19:33,375 --> 00:19:35,125
Curse my hand!

486
00:19:35,291 --> 00:19:36,833
I'd rather be dead

487
00:19:36,875 --> 00:19:37,916
than see Dust-Ali

488
00:19:37,916 --> 00:19:39,708
in this state!

489
00:19:39,708 --> 00:19:42,000
Sir, I beg you! Do something!

490
00:19:42,083 --> 00:19:44,458
A doctor! A medicine! Take him to the hospital!

491
00:19:47,333 --> 00:19:51,583
But which doctor can I call at this hour of the night!

492
00:19:52,166 --> 00:19:53,166
In this condition,

493
00:19:53,208 --> 00:19:56,416
it's not wise to move him anymore!

494
00:19:56,791 --> 00:19:59,583
And we can't take him to the hospital either!

495
00:19:59,791 --> 00:20:02,916
There, they ask questions first!

496
00:20:02,958 --> 00:20:06,541
Asdollah! You explain it!

497
00:20:15,250 --> 00:20:16,583
It seems he wants to say something!

498
00:20:20,166 --> 00:20:21,375
Speak, Dust-Ali.

499
00:20:21,416 --> 00:20:23,000
If you're still alive, say something!

500
00:20:23,041 --> 00:20:25,458
I want Aziz. Where is Aziz?

501
00:20:25,791 --> 00:20:27,083
I'm here, Dust-Ali!

502
00:20:27,083 --> 00:20:29,125
Let me bear your pain!

503
00:20:29,125 --> 00:20:31,666
You... you're not Aziz, I want Aziz.

504
00:20:31,666 --> 00:20:32,250
He wants you!

505
00:20:32,291 --> 00:20:33,375
I want Aziz.

506
00:20:33,541 --> 00:20:35,083
I'm here, Dust-Ali!

507
00:20:35,125 --> 00:20:37,583
Let me bear your pain!

508
00:20:39,625 --> 00:20:40,291
It's me!

509
00:20:40,458 --> 00:20:41,375
It's me myself!

510
00:20:41,541 --> 00:20:44,291
It's me, Aziz, bless that sweet voice of yours!

511
00:20:44,333 --> 00:20:45,708
No! You're not Aziz!

512
00:20:46,166 --> 00:20:47,541
Open your eyes, Dust-Ali!

513
00:20:47,541 --> 00:20:48,166
I want Aziz!

514
00:20:48,166 --> 00:20:49,166
It's me! I'm Aziz!

515
00:20:49,208 --> 00:20:51,166
Please, look at me!

516
00:20:51,208 --> 00:20:52,708
Look! You're not Aziz!-

517
00:20:52,833 --> 00:20:54,208
Ah! God take me!

518
00:20:54,250 --> 00:20:56,458
Dust-Ali doesn't recognize me anymore!

519
00:20:56,916 --> 00:20:57,708
Dust-Ali!

520
00:20:58,208 --> 00:20:59,041
Dust-Ali!

521
00:20:59,291 --> 00:21:00,333
Open your eyes!

522
00:21:00,708 --> 00:21:02,500
I'm Aziz! I'm talking to you!

523
00:21:02,541 --> 00:21:03,083
Me!

524
00:21:03,541 --> 00:21:05,083
Look at me, Dust-Ali!

525
00:21:05,208 --> 00:21:08,583
Dust-Ali, look at me! Please! Thank God I got to see you once more!-

526
00:21:09,583 --> 00:21:10,291
Aziz!

527
00:21:12,250 --> 00:21:13,958
Aziz! Forgive me!

528
00:21:15,625 --> 00:21:16,125
Let...

529
00:21:17,041 --> 00:21:17,583
Let...

530
00:21:18,000 --> 00:21:20,416
Let me die in peace!

531
00:21:21,000 --> 00:21:21,916
Water!

532
00:21:22,458 --> 00:21:23,583
Water!

533
00:21:23,958 --> 00:21:25,125
He wants water, water!

534
00:21:25,333 --> 00:21:26,791
Bring a glass of water!

535
00:21:26,958 --> 00:21:28,500
Mash Ghasem! For God's sake!

536
00:21:30,041 --> 00:21:35,125
Don't let me leave this world thirsty...

537
00:21:39,458 --> 00:21:41,541
Here's the water, Sir. Go ahead, drink up.

538
00:21:43,458 --> 00:21:44,833
To your health.

539
00:21:47,375 --> 00:21:49,583
Peace upon Hossein the martyr, curse upon Yazid.

540
00:21:49,583 --> 00:21:51,166
Watch yourself.

541
00:21:51,833 --> 00:21:53,208
Forgive me.

542
00:21:55,458 --> 00:21:57,125
Aziz, forgive me.

543
00:21:57,291 --> 00:21:58,958
Maybe I

544
00:21:59,250 --> 00:22:01,541
have sinned a great deal!

545
00:22:03,750 --> 00:22:04,041
But...

546
00:22:04,500 --> 00:22:05,791
But Qamar...

547
00:22:07,250 --> 00:22:07,875
Qamar...

548
00:22:09,208 --> 00:22:10,875
Qamar's baby...

549
00:22:12,000 --> 00:22:13,625
Not my fault...

550
00:22:15,333 --> 00:22:17,083
I was blameless...

551
00:22:17,333 --> 00:22:18,875
Where is this Qamar?

552
00:22:18,916 --> 00:22:19,625
Where is she?

553
00:22:19,666 --> 00:22:22,041
In the next room, with the children.

554
00:22:22,166 --> 00:22:23,916
I hope she drops dead,

555
00:22:23,916 --> 00:22:25,916
she's to blame for all of this.

556
00:22:25,916 --> 00:22:28,166
Aziz dear, watch her.

557
00:22:29,041 --> 00:22:30,666
The girl is mad.

558
00:22:31,291 --> 00:22:35,166
To... save the family's honor,

559
00:22:35,333 --> 00:22:37,000
I told her,

560
00:22:37,291 --> 00:22:38,625
Allahverdi,

561
00:22:39,541 --> 00:22:40,541
I...

562
00:22:41,083 --> 00:22:43,291
Not my fault!

563
00:22:43,458 --> 00:22:46,083
Shams-Ali...

564
00:22:46,625 --> 00:22:48,916
Shams-Ali... I'm here, Dust-Ali.-

565
00:22:49,333 --> 00:22:51,125
Sit on the chair.

566
00:22:51,916 --> 00:22:53,000
Shams-Ali...

567
00:22:53,916 --> 00:22:56,250
Pen and paper...

568
00:22:56,291 --> 00:22:57,083
Paper...

569
00:22:58,083 --> 00:22:59,958
Write my will.

570
00:23:00,083 --> 00:23:01,541
Go get paper and bring it... At your service-

571
00:23:01,625 --> 00:23:03,625
Write...

572
00:23:05,000 --> 00:23:07,208
Shams-Ali, write...

573
00:23:07,250 --> 00:23:08,333
Please.

574
00:23:08,333 --> 00:23:10,125
Write: In the name of God.

575
00:23:10,708 --> 00:23:11,958
Write...

576
00:23:12,708 --> 00:23:14,041
All...

577
00:23:14,541 --> 00:23:16,458
all of my property,

578
00:23:17,125 --> 00:23:18,083
belongs...

579
00:23:19,000 --> 00:23:20,166
belongs...

580
00:23:20,208 --> 00:23:22,166
belongs to Aziz!

581
00:23:23,833 --> 00:23:25,958
Let me die!

582
00:23:26,208 --> 00:23:28,416
Aziz won't outlive you,

583
00:23:28,458 --> 00:23:30,375
so why make a will!

584
00:23:38,416 --> 00:23:39,458
Shams-Ali!

585
00:23:39,958 --> 00:23:41,000
Write.

586
00:23:43,208 --> 00:23:45,750
This is my last request.

587
00:23:47,250 --> 00:23:48,583
Whatever I said,

588
00:23:49,416 --> 00:23:50,625
write it.

589
00:23:50,875 --> 00:23:52,708
Man, don't make him lose hope!

590
00:23:52,750 --> 00:23:54,333
God rest him, he was good!

591
00:23:54,875 --> 00:23:55,625
Ghasem!

592
00:23:55,833 --> 00:23:56,833
Come outside.

593
00:23:58,291 --> 00:23:59,458
Why lie, Sir!

594
00:23:59,458 --> 00:24:01,833
You mean, God rest him, he was bad?

595
00:24:01,875 --> 00:24:02,875
Come outside! At your service!-

596
00:24:08,291 --> 00:24:10,291
Write the Tehran house,

597
00:24:11,041 --> 00:24:12,541
the shops,

598
00:24:14,125 --> 00:24:17,875
oh yes, I'd forgotten the Mahmudabad estate!

599
00:24:18,500 --> 00:24:19,875
The entire

600
00:24:20,250 --> 00:24:22,875
Mahmudabad estate in Qazvin,

601
00:24:23,208 --> 00:24:25,416
with its water channel,

602
00:24:27,833 --> 00:24:30,125
to my wife,

603
00:24:33,666 --> 00:24:38,250
I'd rather die than see the Mahmudabad estate!

604
00:24:43,250 --> 00:24:43,708
Dustali!

605
00:24:43,750 --> 00:24:49,125
That Mahmudabad caravanserai was yours too? Huh?

606
00:24:50,750 --> 00:24:53,375
Write the caravanserai too.

607
00:24:53,416 --> 00:24:54,125
Dust-Ali!

608
00:24:54,791 --> 00:24:55,750
The sheep!

609
00:24:56,000 --> 00:24:57,541
Don't forget the poor animals!

610
00:24:57,583 --> 00:24:59,125
They'll die of thirst!

611
00:24:59,125 --> 00:25:01,791
Damn the sheep!

612
00:25:02,125 --> 00:25:04,583
He sold the sheep last year!

613
00:25:04,625 --> 00:25:05,125
Oh?!

614
00:25:06,291 --> 00:25:07,500
What a pity!

615
00:25:07,541 --> 00:25:08,625
I wish you'd left them in your will

616
00:25:08,666 --> 00:25:10,583
to Shir-Ali the butcher's wife!

617
00:25:10,750 --> 00:25:12,375
Asdollah, stop it!

618
00:25:12,583 --> 00:25:14,208
This is no time for joking!

619
00:25:17,416 --> 00:25:19,000
Now give it so I can sign it.

620
00:25:19,000 --> 00:25:19,625
Give it.

621
00:25:19,666 --> 00:25:19,916
Here.

622
00:25:20,041 --> 00:25:21,250
Take it, sign it.

623
00:25:21,458 --> 00:25:23,791
Your signature must be on it too. All right.-

624
00:25:23,833 --> 00:25:25,833
Everyone's signature. Here's the pen, and here's the will.-

625
00:25:25,875 --> 00:25:26,791
Here, sign.

626
00:25:26,791 --> 00:25:28,458
Sign... Sign it, Dust-Ali.-

627
00:25:28,500 --> 00:25:29,041
Sign.

628
00:25:29,083 --> 00:25:30,125
O God!

629
00:25:30,875 --> 00:25:32,833
Give me strength...

630
00:25:33,166 --> 00:25:34,500
Give me strength...

631
00:25:34,916 --> 00:25:37,208
that I may sign this.

632
00:25:37,500 --> 00:25:41,083
Bring my hand out from under the blanket.

633
00:25:41,125 --> 00:25:42,083
Bring it out.

634
00:25:42,333 --> 00:25:42,791
Easy.

635
00:25:45,541 --> 00:25:45,958
Here.

636
00:25:48,208 --> 00:25:49,083
Take it.

637
00:25:49,416 --> 00:25:50,875
Sign. Watch out-

638
00:25:52,291 --> 00:25:53,333
Oh, dear God...

639
00:25:53,375 --> 00:25:54,166
Here, hold it like this.

640
00:25:54,208 --> 00:25:55,291
Give me strength,

641
00:25:55,333 --> 00:25:56,291
so I may sign.

642
00:25:56,333 --> 00:25:56,750
Sign.

643
00:25:56,791 --> 00:25:57,708
Dear God!

644
00:25:58,375 --> 00:25:59,250
Give me strength!

645
00:26:00,000 --> 00:26:01,791
So I may sign this. Here, my dear, take it.-

646
00:26:01,833 --> 00:26:02,833
God! Sign it.-

647
00:26:02,833 --> 00:26:04,291
Dear God, oh! Hold it just like this.-

648
00:26:04,291 --> 00:26:05,250
Ow... Sign it!-

649
00:26:05,333 --> 00:26:06,708
(Dust-Ali shouts)

650
00:26:06,750 --> 00:26:07,333
Sign it.

651
00:26:07,375 --> 00:26:08,791
Ow, my hand!

652
00:26:08,833 --> 00:26:10,708
Ow, my hand, dear God! Hold it tight!-

653
00:26:10,708 --> 00:26:11,375
My hand!

654
00:26:11,666 --> 00:26:14,000
They've broken my hand, dear God!

655
00:26:14,041 --> 00:26:15,416
Let go of my hand! Hold it like this!-

656
00:26:15,416 --> 00:26:16,416
Let go! Easy!-

657
00:26:17,250 --> 00:26:18,041
Watch out!

658
00:26:18,041 --> 00:26:20,125
Oh! Dear God, my hand!

659
00:26:20,166 --> 00:26:22,833
My hand! God! My hand! God! Let go!

660
00:26:23,083 --> 00:26:27,041
Sign already! Sign, damn you! (Dust-Ali screams)

661
00:26:27,083 --> 00:26:27,833
Sign!

662
00:26:27,875 --> 00:26:31,041
(Dust-Ali screams)

663
00:26:31,041 --> 00:26:31,708
Sir!

664
00:26:33,000 --> 00:26:33,708
Please come!

665
00:26:38,375 --> 00:26:40,875
They're killing this poor man, Sir!

666
00:26:41,416 --> 00:26:42,416
Hurry!-

667
00:26:43,875 --> 00:26:46,125
My hand! My hand!

668
00:26:46,125 --> 00:26:48,250
Oh, my hand! God!

669
00:26:48,291 --> 00:26:49,625
What's the matter with you?

670
00:26:49,625 --> 00:26:52,041
You've broken my hand! Leave him alone!-

671
00:26:52,041 --> 00:26:54,208
Lady Aziz! Go in with Qamar!

672
00:26:54,708 --> 00:26:56,708
Oh, dear God...

673
00:26:59,541 --> 00:27:00,625
Don't be upset, Sir!

674
00:27:00,666 --> 00:27:02,041
They're husband and wife, after all!

675
00:27:02,500 --> 00:27:03,541
Uncle Asdollah! Hmm?-

676
00:27:03,791 --> 00:27:04,458
Uncle Asdollah!

677
00:27:06,291 --> 00:27:06,833
Uncle Asdollah!

678
00:27:06,875 --> 00:27:08,666
Are you upset because of Dust-Ali Khan?

679
00:27:08,708 --> 00:27:09,750
It's all a lie!

680
00:27:09,875 --> 00:27:11,250
I'm sure, out of fear of Lady Aziz,

681
00:27:11,291 --> 00:27:13,041
he had the doctor bandage him head to toe! Moment!-

682
00:27:13,041 --> 00:27:14,375
I know!

683
00:27:14,416 --> 00:27:16,291
This family is cursed, boy!

684
00:27:16,500 --> 00:27:18,541
Tomorrow a new quarrel starts!

685
00:27:20,125 --> 00:27:21,541
Moment, Lady Aziz! What is it?-

686
00:27:21,958 --> 00:27:22,625
Dust-Ali,

687
00:27:22,666 --> 00:27:24,416
even if his whole body gets well,

688
00:27:24,458 --> 00:27:26,541
this right hand won't move anymore!

689
00:27:27,041 --> 00:27:28,333
Poor Dust-Ali!

690
00:27:28,541 --> 00:27:29,375
Well, obviously!

691
00:27:29,416 --> 00:27:31,583
When a bullet hits the rear,

692
00:27:31,791 --> 00:27:33,708
your right hand gets paralyzed!

693
00:27:33,708 --> 00:27:35,333
Shut up, shameless!

694
00:27:36,208 --> 00:27:38,166
At your service, mademoiselle!

695
00:27:39,458 --> 00:27:40,375
Did you see today

696
00:27:40,375 --> 00:27:42,625
how Dear Uncle snapped at your Agha Joon?

697
00:27:42,666 --> 00:27:43,166
Yes!

698
00:27:43,583 --> 00:27:44,666
I remember at Dear Uncle's house,

699
00:27:44,708 --> 00:27:46,250
when you were talking with Qamar,

700
00:27:46,291 --> 00:27:48,208
Dear Uncle said some things about origin and lineage.

701
00:27:48,208 --> 00:27:48,750
And once last night too,

702
00:27:48,750 --> 00:27:50,083
when Dust-Ali Khan had been shot.

703
00:27:50,416 --> 00:27:52,416
Each time I saw such a flash of rage in your father's eyes

704
00:27:52,416 --> 00:27:53,083
that I was sure

705
00:27:53,125 --> 00:27:55,375
he'll bring fresh misery on this old man tomorrow.

706
00:27:55,791 --> 00:27:57,416
My Agha Joon hasn't vanished for nothing!

707
00:27:57,416 --> 00:27:59,250
I'm sure right now he's thinking only

708
00:27:59,250 --> 00:28:01,375
of how to repay Dear Uncle's insults!

709
00:28:01,708 --> 00:28:04,458
Any day now he'll take up his plots again!

710
00:28:04,458 --> 00:28:05,083
You can be sure

711
00:28:05,125 --> 00:28:07,000
that your Agha Joon's new plot has started!

712
00:28:07,250 --> 00:28:08,458
but on the sly!

713
00:28:09,041 --> 00:28:10,791
If the matter of Qamar's pregnancy hadn't come up,

714
00:28:10,833 --> 00:28:12,291
your Agha Joon would have started this very night!

715
00:28:12,458 --> 00:28:14,208
Both sides are ridiculous!

716
00:28:14,750 --> 00:28:16,166
These people talk of origin and lineage

717
00:28:16,166 --> 00:28:18,250
as if everyone else hatched from an egg!

718
00:28:20,916 --> 00:28:21,291
Saeed!

719
00:28:21,916 --> 00:28:22,500
If you can,

720
00:28:22,500 --> 00:28:24,125
that paper your Dear Uncle wrote to Hitler,

721
00:28:24,166 --> 00:28:25,250
be sure to swipe it!

722
00:28:25,333 --> 00:28:26,208
So far I haven't been able...

723
00:28:26,250 --> 00:28:26,958
Try, try.

724
00:29:03,333 --> 00:29:04,041
Sir!

725
00:29:04,750 --> 00:29:05,458
Leili!

726
00:29:08,666 --> 00:29:09,416
Is no one home?

727
00:29:12,166 --> 00:29:14,125
(Dust-Ali starts moaning)

728
00:29:16,166 --> 00:29:16,916
Don't be afraid!

729
00:29:17,125 --> 00:29:17,791
It's me!

730
00:29:17,833 --> 00:29:18,750
Eat!

731
00:29:18,833 --> 00:29:20,416
Stuff that damned belly of yours!

732
00:29:20,416 --> 00:29:21,208
Get up!

733
00:29:21,875 --> 00:29:22,958
Get up, stuff your face!

734
00:29:23,583 --> 00:29:24,166
Get up!

735
00:29:24,958 --> 00:29:26,500
God knows, I'm in a bad way!

736
00:29:26,833 --> 00:29:27,833
The doctor said,

737
00:29:27,833 --> 00:29:30,500
to make up for the blood that's gone from my body,

738
00:29:30,750 --> 00:29:33,333
I must eat something, no matter what!

739
00:29:33,750 --> 00:29:35,541
What can I do? I'm hungry!

740
00:29:36,250 --> 00:29:38,458
But please, don't tell Aziz!

741
00:29:38,916 --> 00:29:42,166
I swear by your death, I'm dying of pain right now!

742
00:29:42,166 --> 00:29:43,416
Your father's death!

743
00:29:43,458 --> 00:29:44,666
Why my death?

744
00:29:44,708 --> 00:29:45,666
You went to San Francisco,

745
00:29:45,708 --> 00:29:47,333
you have to bear the trouble too!

746
00:29:47,750 --> 00:29:48,833
On my life!

747
00:29:48,916 --> 00:29:51,375
I swear by your death, I didn't do anything.

748
00:29:51,541 --> 00:29:54,083
I only feel sorry for this girl!

749
00:29:54,458 --> 00:29:55,250
Get lost!

750
00:29:55,291 --> 00:29:56,791
Yeah, right!

751
00:29:58,625 --> 00:30:00,500
Tell me, why did you call?

752
00:30:00,541 --> 00:30:01,583
I have to go to the office.

753
00:30:01,833 --> 00:30:02,791
Look, Asdollah!

754
00:30:02,958 --> 00:30:04,916
If anyone turns up, I want

755
00:30:05,250 --> 00:30:06,666
to marry Qamar off!

756
00:30:07,083 --> 00:30:10,208
Even if he only marries her for a few days and...

757
00:30:11,125 --> 00:30:12,541
I'll sign a pledge

758
00:30:12,583 --> 00:30:14,458
that I'll keep the baby myself.

759
00:30:14,916 --> 00:30:15,708
Moment!

760
00:30:15,750 --> 00:30:17,083
You won't find a fool

761
00:30:17,125 --> 00:30:18,666
who'd take on this girl, even for one hour,

762
00:30:18,708 --> 00:30:20,500
and saddle himself with her!

763
00:30:20,500 --> 00:30:21,375
Look, Asdollah!

764
00:30:21,916 --> 00:30:23,083
I thought that...

765
00:30:23,125 --> 00:30:25,541
I mean, I thought to myself...

766
00:30:26,375 --> 00:30:27,541
I said,

767
00:30:27,583 --> 00:30:28,875
if you

768
00:30:28,875 --> 00:30:29,625
were willing...

769
00:30:29,666 --> 00:30:31,250
Moment! Moment!

770
00:30:31,833 --> 00:30:33,666
This'll cost you, Dust-Ali!

771
00:30:33,708 --> 00:30:36,250
You'll have to loosen the purse strings!

772
00:30:36,416 --> 00:30:38,166
You want all of Qamar's inheritance for yourself?

773
00:30:38,208 --> 00:30:39,458
Whatever you want, I'll give you!

774
00:30:39,958 --> 00:30:41,041
Look, Asdollah!

775
00:30:41,166 --> 00:30:43,958
You and I grew up together.

776
00:30:44,791 --> 00:30:48,125
Setting aside these petty, childish differences,

777
00:30:48,125 --> 00:30:50,250
you and I have always helped each other.

778
00:30:50,250 --> 00:30:51,916
We've been friends.

779
00:30:52,458 --> 00:30:53,875
Believe me, Asdollah dear!

780
00:30:54,583 --> 00:30:57,500
I don't have long to live, brother.

781
00:30:57,916 --> 00:30:58,958
Today I die.

782
00:30:59,291 --> 00:31:00,541
Or tomorrow!

783
00:31:01,250 --> 00:31:03,000
In short, I'm like a lamp, ah!-

784
00:31:03,000 --> 00:31:04,875
that's flickering, and any moment

785
00:31:04,875 --> 00:31:06,541
may go out!

786
00:31:06,750 --> 00:31:08,291
Don't say it, Dust-Ali!

787
00:31:08,708 --> 00:31:10,750
This is my last request of you!

788
00:31:11,041 --> 00:31:13,000
Don't say that, you're breaking my heart!

789
00:31:13,041 --> 00:31:14,125
You, so young!

790
00:31:14,125 --> 00:31:15,333
With so many dreams!

791
00:31:16,125 --> 00:31:17,708
I promise you!

792
00:31:17,875 --> 00:31:20,000
Every Thursday night, a bunch of hollyhocks

793
00:31:20,041 --> 00:31:21,458
I'll put on your gravestone!

794
00:31:21,833 --> 00:31:23,000
Rest easy!

795
00:31:23,041 --> 00:31:23,583
Asdollah?!

796
00:31:24,041 --> 00:31:25,791
Is this any time for joking?

797
00:31:25,833 --> 00:31:26,708
I'm not joking!

798
00:31:27,041 --> 00:31:28,500
Don't joke!

799
00:31:28,500 --> 00:31:29,625
Say how much you want!

800
00:31:29,625 --> 00:31:30,916
Whatever you want, I'll give you!

801
00:31:31,625 --> 00:31:34,291
I know your office salary doesn't go far!

802
00:31:34,291 --> 00:31:35,291
Say it, dear!

803
00:31:35,666 --> 00:31:36,250
Go on!

804
00:31:36,958 --> 00:31:38,208
You'll give however much I want?

805
00:31:38,375 --> 00:31:40,000
For the sake of saving this girl!

806
00:31:40,166 --> 00:31:42,125
For our family's honor!

807
00:31:42,125 --> 00:31:43,916
Whatever you want, I'll give you!

808
00:31:43,958 --> 00:31:45,666
You just tell me how much you want!

809
00:31:47,500 --> 00:31:50,333
The Mahmudabad estate, dear Dust-Ali!

810
00:31:50,625 --> 00:31:51,250
What?!

811
00:31:52,000 --> 00:31:53,458
The Mahmudabad estate?!

812
00:31:54,416 --> 00:31:55,666
Have you gone mad?

813
00:31:57,041 --> 00:31:59,958
Me, give you a whole estate?!

814
00:32:00,625 --> 00:32:02,958
Just so you'll marry this girl?

815
00:32:03,166 --> 00:32:04,625
Have I lost my mind?

816
00:32:04,791 --> 00:32:06,083
Moment!

817
00:32:06,166 --> 00:32:07,750
Moment, Dust-Ali!

818
00:32:07,791 --> 00:32:10,041
Me, give you the Mahmudabad estate?!

819
00:32:10,083 --> 00:32:12,458
Just so you'll marry Qamar for two days?

820
00:32:12,750 --> 00:32:15,666
Moment, dear Dust-Ali Khan!

821
00:32:15,750 --> 00:32:17,916
I liked you very much, Dust-Ali,

822
00:32:17,958 --> 00:32:20,041
I sat here, quiet and calm,

823
00:32:20,083 --> 00:32:21,583
and listened to you!

824
00:32:22,916 --> 00:32:24,708
You were a very good man,

825
00:32:24,750 --> 00:32:26,916
that I came as soon as you called!

826
00:32:27,500 --> 00:32:30,208
But I must do Azrael's job early,

827
00:32:30,250 --> 00:32:31,458
so that you, you lowlife,

828
00:32:31,625 --> 00:32:33,250
stop talking such nonsense!

829
00:32:34,125 --> 00:32:35,083
O Lord!

830
00:32:35,125 --> 00:32:35,958
Forgive me!

831
00:32:36,833 --> 00:32:38,833
I've never hurt so much as an ant!

832
00:32:39,541 --> 00:32:40,541
But this man,

833
00:32:40,666 --> 00:32:42,750
the sooner he joins You,

834
00:32:42,875 --> 00:32:44,083
the better for humanity!

835
00:32:47,125 --> 00:32:48,000
O God!

836
00:32:48,583 --> 00:32:49,625
Help me!

837
00:32:50,250 --> 00:32:51,250
Dust-Ali!

838
00:32:51,875 --> 00:32:52,875
As a friend,

839
00:32:52,916 --> 00:32:54,750
I want to do you the greatest favor!

840
00:32:54,791 --> 00:32:55,250
Asdollah!

841
00:32:55,375 --> 00:32:56,333
On your life,

842
00:32:56,416 --> 00:32:58,250
I swear, I was joking!

843
00:32:58,333 --> 00:33:00,083
By God I was joking, Asdollah!

844
00:33:00,125 --> 00:33:02,666
On your life! I swear, I was joking!

845
00:33:02,791 --> 00:33:04,166
Every minute you stay in this world,

846
00:33:04,208 --> 00:33:06,291
adds another sin to your list!

847
00:33:06,791 --> 00:33:09,458
See you on Judgment Day, dear Dust-Ali!

848
00:33:09,500 --> 00:33:10,916
Asdollah! Dust-Ali!-

849
00:33:10,916 --> 00:33:11,791
I'm choking!

850
00:33:11,833 --> 00:33:12,666
To hell!

851
00:33:12,708 --> 00:33:13,291
I'm choking!

852
00:33:13,333 --> 00:33:14,125
To hell with it!

853
00:33:14,125 --> 00:33:15,625
I'm choking!

854
00:33:16,083 --> 00:33:17,083
To hell with it!

855
00:33:17,125 --> 00:33:18,375
Ow! I'm dying!

856
00:33:18,666 --> 00:33:21,083
Heartless! You hit my wounds!

857
00:33:21,083 --> 00:33:22,083
Idiot!

858
00:33:26,083 --> 00:33:28,125
I thought you expected me to find someone

859
00:33:28,166 --> 00:33:29,708
to marry the girl you ruined!

860
00:33:29,875 --> 00:33:32,375
Even at death's door, you can't stop being vile!

861
00:33:32,833 --> 00:33:34,833
You lowlife make a filthy mess,

862
00:33:35,083 --> 00:33:36,750
and I have to clean it up?

863
00:33:37,125 --> 00:33:38,041
Wretch!

864
00:33:38,208 --> 00:33:39,791
In all your misery, you got lucky

865
00:33:39,833 --> 00:33:41,791
that your wife shot that battered backside of yours!

866
00:33:41,958 --> 00:33:44,541
Honestly, you'd have gotten 15 years in prison for this!

867
00:33:44,583 --> 00:33:46,041
How else can I say it!

868
00:33:46,750 --> 00:33:49,666
Believe me! On your life, I didn't do it!

869
00:33:49,708 --> 00:33:51,791
On my life! On your life!

870
00:33:51,916 --> 00:33:52,750
On your own life!

871
00:33:52,958 --> 00:33:54,083
On your ancestors' graves!

872
00:33:54,541 --> 00:33:55,791
You jackass!

873
00:33:58,291 --> 00:33:58,833
What happened?

874
00:34:00,250 --> 00:34:01,500
Hello, Uncle Asdollah!

875
00:34:02,833 --> 00:34:03,583
What happened?

876
00:34:05,583 --> 00:34:07,208
Nothing's happened, Leili dear!

877
00:34:07,833 --> 00:34:10,041
That ass Dust-Ali is on his way to the other world!

878
00:34:10,375 --> 00:34:12,458
Right now he's chasing the doorkeeper's wife in hell!

879
00:34:13,166 --> 00:34:15,791
You're lucky I can't get up!

880
00:34:15,875 --> 00:34:17,500
I swear I'd give you such a beating

881
00:34:17,500 --> 00:34:18,875
that you'd never forget it as long as you live!

882
00:34:19,291 --> 00:34:20,583
Pity I can't get up!

883
00:34:20,750 --> 00:34:21,208
Shut up!

884
00:34:24,583 --> 00:34:25,625
How's he doing?

885
00:34:25,916 --> 00:34:27,541
He's flirting with Azrael!

886
00:34:27,541 --> 00:34:28,291
Asdollah!

887
00:34:28,333 --> 00:34:30,791
I don't think now is the time for joking!

888
00:34:30,833 --> 00:34:31,833
I'm not joking either, Sir!

889
00:34:31,875 --> 00:34:32,625
Apparently, fortunately,

890
00:34:32,625 --> 00:34:34,583
the bullet has put his noble member out of work!

891
00:34:34,708 --> 00:34:35,750
Of course it's our own fault!

892
00:34:35,750 --> 00:34:37,916
If that time we'd let Lady Aziz cut it off,

893
00:34:38,125 --> 00:34:39,916
we wouldn't have wasted a bullet this time!

894
00:34:41,708 --> 00:34:42,833
What was that about?

895
00:34:42,958 --> 00:34:44,000
Nothing, Father!

896
00:34:44,000 --> 00:34:44,416
Uncle Asdollah

897
00:34:44,458 --> 00:34:46,125
always jokes with Dust-Ali Khan!

898
00:34:46,166 --> 00:34:47,625
All right! You go in with Qamar.

899
00:34:47,666 --> 00:34:49,541
I have to talk with Dust-Ali a little.

900
00:34:51,833 --> 00:34:53,833
♪ Homayoun Piece – Composed by Morteza Mahjubi ♪

901
00:35:02,166 --> 00:35:04,083
Knit one, purl one.

902
00:35:04,125 --> 00:35:07,416
Knit one, purl one.

903
00:35:07,416 --> 00:35:09,291
Knit one...

904
00:35:10,375 --> 00:35:11,708
Qamar? Purl one...-

905
00:35:16,708 --> 00:35:19,458
Knit one,

906
00:35:20,000 --> 00:35:21,416
purl one.

907
00:35:22,166 --> 00:35:23,125
Dust-Ali!

908
00:35:23,958 --> 00:35:26,416
When I ask you something,

909
00:35:26,500 --> 00:35:27,500
I expect,

910
00:35:27,500 --> 00:35:30,541
for the sake of the kindnesses I've done you,

911
00:35:31,375 --> 00:35:33,750
that you answer me with sincerity.

912
00:35:35,541 --> 00:35:36,041
Well...

913
00:35:36,166 --> 00:35:38,333
To err is human.

914
00:35:39,125 --> 00:35:40,625
I swear on your life,

915
00:35:40,916 --> 00:35:42,166
on Aziz's life!

916
00:35:42,208 --> 00:35:44,041
I swear by my father's soul!

917
00:35:44,291 --> 00:35:45,333
I am blameless.

918
00:35:45,375 --> 00:35:45,875
Dust-Ali!

919
00:35:45,916 --> 00:35:47,791
Watch your words!

920
00:35:48,000 --> 00:35:49,916
Last night I felt

921
00:35:49,958 --> 00:35:52,791
that you wanted to say some things to me!

922
00:35:53,541 --> 00:35:56,666
But those it didn't suit

923
00:35:56,916 --> 00:35:58,125
didn't let you!

924
00:35:58,625 --> 00:36:01,208
Now say, what did you want to tell me?

925
00:36:01,333 --> 00:36:02,250
I... I... I... I...

926
00:36:02,416 --> 00:36:03,458
In fact...

927
00:36:03,583 --> 00:36:04,958
Maybe you're right!

928
00:36:05,208 --> 00:36:07,500
I wanted to say I'm innocent!

929
00:36:08,041 --> 00:36:10,416
And I'm ready now, whatever the price,

930
00:36:10,708 --> 00:36:11,833
whatever it takes,

931
00:36:11,875 --> 00:36:13,125
to smooth things over!

932
00:36:13,541 --> 00:36:15,083
Listen, Dust-Ali!

933
00:36:15,333 --> 00:36:17,083
As Napoleon says:

934
00:36:17,333 --> 00:36:21,125
Between traitor and loyal servant

935
00:36:21,541 --> 00:36:22,833
is one step!

936
00:36:23,041 --> 00:36:24,166
The important thing is

937
00:36:24,250 --> 00:36:27,166
that you take that one step at the right time!

938
00:36:27,666 --> 00:36:31,250
If you're sorry now and want to make amends,

939
00:36:31,250 --> 00:36:32,791
I'll help you.

940
00:36:33,083 --> 00:36:34,333
Tell me the truth.

941
00:36:34,750 --> 00:36:37,250
I've recently realized

942
00:36:37,416 --> 00:36:39,791
that you support

943
00:36:39,958 --> 00:36:41,291
certain policies.

944
00:36:41,791 --> 00:36:42,541
Me?!

945
00:36:43,291 --> 00:36:44,291
Politics?

946
00:36:45,041 --> 00:36:46,000
I thought

947
00:36:46,041 --> 00:36:49,166
you were asking me about the matter of Qamar!

948
00:36:49,458 --> 00:36:50,875
What do I have to do with politics! How's he doing?-

949
00:36:51,166 --> 00:36:52,333
Hasn't he come to yet?

950
00:36:53,375 --> 00:36:54,000
Say he's asleep!

951
00:36:59,208 --> 00:37:01,625
How is my poor Dust-Ali?

952
00:37:02,000 --> 00:37:04,000
Hush!

953
00:37:04,458 --> 00:37:05,250
Easy!

954
00:37:05,250 --> 00:37:05,958
He's asleep!

955
00:37:07,875 --> 00:37:09,208
Thank God!

956
00:37:09,583 --> 00:37:12,125
It seems the danger is passing!

957
00:37:12,125 --> 00:37:14,083
From your lips to God's ears!

958
00:37:15,041 --> 00:37:16,583
I've vowed, if Dust-Ali gets well,

959
00:37:16,625 --> 00:37:18,625
I'll sacrifice a sheep at Emamzadeh Davud!

960
00:37:19,291 --> 00:37:20,583
He's getting well.

961
00:37:20,750 --> 00:37:22,625
Rest easy.

962
00:37:23,333 --> 00:37:25,500
What's your plan for Qamar?

963
00:37:27,500 --> 00:37:29,166
I just saw another doctor.

964
00:37:29,208 --> 00:37:30,083
Well, what did he say?

965
00:37:31,333 --> 00:37:33,541
He said, to get rid of the baby,

966
00:37:34,291 --> 00:37:35,625
it's already too late!

967
00:37:36,125 --> 00:37:37,583
It may be dangerous for her.

968
00:37:37,625 --> 00:37:39,958
Doctors always say this nonsense!

969
00:37:39,958 --> 00:37:42,500
Why don't you take her to one of these midwives?

970
00:37:44,458 --> 00:37:45,750
Sir, I'm truly afraid!

971
00:37:45,916 --> 00:37:47,375
I'm afraid, God forbid,

972
00:37:47,833 --> 00:37:50,333
something terrible will happen to this poor girl!

973
00:37:51,000 --> 00:37:54,916
You people don't think of family honor!

974
00:37:55,208 --> 00:37:57,833
Her poor father, if he were alive,

975
00:37:57,833 --> 00:37:59,750
would have died of grief by now!

976
00:38:00,041 --> 00:38:04,041
Thank God he died and didn't see this shame!

977
00:38:04,791 --> 00:38:07,416
The news of it will spread everywhere.

978
00:38:07,458 --> 00:38:09,375
People will gossip.

979
00:38:09,791 --> 00:38:11,625
That's exactly what I'm afraid of! Oh!-

980
00:38:11,916 --> 00:38:13,958
Surely it's reached many ears!

981
00:38:14,750 --> 00:38:17,583
And that wretch can't keep his mouth shut!

982
00:38:18,041 --> 00:38:19,958
I promise you that any day now,

983
00:38:19,958 --> 00:38:21,041
that,

984
00:38:21,041 --> 00:38:22,208
that old crow,

985
00:38:22,541 --> 00:38:24,166
Farrokh-Laqa herself will turn up,

986
00:38:24,208 --> 00:38:25,041
with that nayeb...

987
00:38:25,708 --> 00:38:27,750
Nayeb Teymour Khan will turn up around here!

988
00:38:27,916 --> 00:38:28,458
Nayeb?

989
00:38:29,250 --> 00:38:31,250
Nayeb Teymour Khan, why?

990
00:38:33,250 --> 00:38:35,875
This morning the head of the criminal branch telephoned.

991
00:38:36,166 --> 00:38:37,958
The one I went to see that time.

992
00:38:38,250 --> 00:38:39,458
My late husband's friend!

993
00:38:40,250 --> 00:38:43,000
He was saying that last night an unknown person telephoned,

994
00:38:43,083 --> 00:38:45,541
told him that I shot Dust-Ali,

995
00:38:45,750 --> 00:38:46,875
now he's wounded,

996
00:38:46,916 --> 00:38:49,333
I've brought him and hidden him at your place.

997
00:38:52,041 --> 00:38:53,000
It's their work!

998
00:38:53,333 --> 00:38:54,291
It's their own work!

999
00:38:54,625 --> 00:38:55,500
Whose work?

1000
00:38:55,666 --> 00:38:57,458
The English!

1001
00:38:58,000 --> 00:38:59,125
That very night,

1002
00:38:59,166 --> 00:39:02,208
when that Indian Sardar came into the doctor's office,

1003
00:39:02,250 --> 00:39:03,500
I understood!

1004
00:39:04,041 --> 00:39:04,875
Didn't he say?!

1005
00:39:04,958 --> 00:39:08,416
Didn't he say whether the caller had a special accent?

1006
00:39:09,125 --> 00:39:11,208
Yes! But he didn't say an Indian accent!

1007
00:39:11,500 --> 00:39:12,958
Then... then what?

1008
00:39:13,208 --> 00:39:14,833
He said the one who telephoned him,

1009
00:39:14,875 --> 00:39:16,208
had a husky voice.

1010
00:39:16,333 --> 00:39:17,625
What? What was it?

1011
00:39:18,166 --> 00:39:19,291
Husky!

1012
00:39:20,708 --> 00:39:22,000
Husky?

1013
00:39:22,958 --> 00:39:24,958
♪ traditional music ♪

1014
00:40:03,500 --> 00:40:05,166
That day, in Dear Uncle's face,

1015
00:40:05,208 --> 00:40:07,916
the fate of my love looking darker than ever.

1016
00:40:09,083 --> 00:40:10,666
My fear was not without reason.

1017
00:40:11,166 --> 00:40:14,291
The only person in our family who had a husky voice

1018
00:40:14,958 --> 00:40:15,916
was Agha Jan!

1019
00:40:26,583 --> 00:40:28,583
(sound of the telephone ringing)

1020
00:40:34,458 --> 00:40:35,083
Hello!

1021
00:40:35,416 --> 00:40:36,125
Uncle Asdollah!

1022
00:40:36,583 --> 00:40:37,291
Uncle Asdollah!

1023
00:40:37,541 --> 00:40:38,583
Come here quick!

1024
00:40:38,750 --> 00:40:39,500
Is that you, Saeed?

1025
00:40:40,125 --> 00:40:40,666
What is it?

1026
00:40:41,083 --> 00:40:42,000
What's happened?

1027
00:40:42,583 --> 00:40:43,541
It can't be said on the telephone!

1028
00:40:43,541 --> 00:40:45,250
For God's sake, come here quickly!

1029
00:40:46,333 --> 00:40:48,833
If you don't come, I think something will happen again!

1030
00:40:49,041 --> 00:40:49,958
Dear Uncle has understood that Agha Joon

1031
00:40:49,958 --> 00:40:51,500
telephoned the police chief!

1032
00:40:51,500 --> 00:40:53,000
Moment! Moment!

1033
00:40:53,041 --> 00:40:54,208
I don't understand what you're saying?!

1034
00:40:54,208 --> 00:40:55,041
What telephone?

1035
00:40:55,250 --> 00:40:57,333
I think someone's making trouble again!

1036
00:40:57,625 --> 00:40:59,416
Someone telephoned the police chief.

1037
00:40:59,458 --> 00:41:00,250
He told him about last night,

1038
00:41:00,250 --> 00:41:00,916
how Lady Aziz-os-Saltaneh

1039
00:41:00,916 --> 00:41:02,083
shot Dust-Ali Khan,

1040
00:41:02,083 --> 00:41:03,166
the whole story!

1041
00:41:03,166 --> 00:41:05,375
Now they want to send an officer to investigate!

1042
00:41:05,625 --> 00:41:07,750
That fellow Nayeb Teymour Khan

1043
00:41:07,750 --> 00:41:09,125
might show up around here again!

1044
00:41:09,708 --> 00:41:10,375
Dear Uncle,

1045
00:41:10,416 --> 00:41:11,875
since they found out this is Agha Joon's doing,

1046
00:41:11,916 --> 00:41:12,916
has gone mad!

1047
00:41:13,458 --> 00:41:15,375
How did they figure out it was your Agha Joon?

1048
00:41:15,500 --> 00:41:17,000
But the fellow's voice was husky!

1049
00:41:17,333 --> 00:41:18,500
The police chief...

1050
00:41:19,625 --> 00:41:21,458
The police chief told Lady Aziz-os-Saltaneh,

1051
00:41:21,500 --> 00:41:23,208
the fellow had a hus-

1052
00:41:23,291 --> 00:41:25,375
(the Shazdeh laughs)

1053
00:41:25,708 --> 00:41:27,041
Oh, good grief!

1054
00:41:27,041 --> 00:41:28,875
Last night, when Dear Uncle snapped at your father,

1055
00:41:28,916 --> 00:41:31,583
I knew your father would stir up trouble!

1056
00:41:31,666 --> 00:41:32,958
Nobody told him, 'Look, man,'

1057
00:41:33,000 --> 00:41:34,791
'you could've held a handkerchief over your mouth!'

1058
00:41:35,291 --> 00:41:36,041
Uncle Asdollah!

1059
00:41:36,291 --> 00:41:37,791
Get here quickly!

1060
00:41:38,250 --> 00:41:39,000
I think Dear Uncle

1061
00:41:39,041 --> 00:41:39,958
has arranged to go this afternoon

1062
00:41:40,000 --> 00:41:41,333
to see the police chief!

1063
00:41:41,875 --> 00:41:43,083
Then I won't come there now!

1064
00:41:43,166 --> 00:41:45,250
Better that I see the police chief first!

1065
00:41:45,541 --> 00:41:47,458
Our office chief is related to him.

1066
00:41:47,500 --> 00:41:48,333
This way is much better.

1067
00:41:48,708 --> 00:41:50,250
What will you do there?!

1068
00:41:50,958 --> 00:41:51,958
How thick you are, boy!

1069
00:41:52,583 --> 00:41:53,958
Before your Dear Uncle gets there,

1070
00:41:53,958 --> 00:41:55,583
I'll go see the police chief,

1071
00:41:55,916 --> 00:41:57,333
tell him it was a family matter.

1072
00:41:57,416 --> 00:41:59,083
Maybe I can whitewash the whole thing!

1073
00:41:59,375 --> 00:42:00,958
Uncle Asdollah! I beg you!

1074
00:42:01,125 --> 00:42:01,541
If today,

1075
00:42:01,583 --> 00:42:03,500
a fight breaks out between Agha Joon and Dear Uncle,

1076
00:42:03,666 --> 00:42:05,833
I won't be able to see Leili again!

1077
00:42:05,875 --> 00:42:06,458
Ugh!

1078
00:42:06,458 --> 00:42:08,125
You and your Leili this, Leili that!

1079
00:42:08,250 --> 00:42:08,958
I've told you a hundred times,

1080
00:42:09,000 --> 00:42:10,958
go to San Francisco with her, child!

1081
00:42:11,458 --> 00:42:12,833
and be done with it!

1082
00:42:13,500 --> 00:42:14,416
Ugh!

1083
00:42:14,458 --> 00:42:15,958
Uncle Asdollah! You've started again?!

1084
00:42:17,625 --> 00:42:18,458
Uncle Asdollah!

1085
00:42:40,041 --> 00:42:41,500
Leili dear, good news!

1086
00:42:41,791 --> 00:42:42,916
Good news!

1087
00:42:43,000 --> 00:42:44,583
Leili dear, I bring good news!

1088
00:42:44,625 --> 00:42:45,291
What happened, Dear Uncle?

1089
00:42:45,333 --> 00:42:45,958
Good news!

1090
00:42:47,583 --> 00:42:50,500
Dear Puri telegraphed, he's doing very well.

1091
00:42:50,541 --> 00:42:52,333
Arriving tomorrow night by train.

1092
00:42:52,791 --> 00:42:55,000
I ran here from the telegraph office

1093
00:42:55,125 --> 00:42:57,250
to tell Khan Dadash!

1094
00:42:57,375 --> 00:42:58,458
Good news!

1095
00:42:58,500 --> 00:42:59,875
Father isn't home.

1096
00:43:01,666 --> 00:43:02,583
Has he gone somewhere?

1097
00:43:02,708 --> 00:43:04,000
With Lady Aziz-os-Saltaneh

1098
00:43:04,000 --> 00:43:05,458
they've gone to the police chief.

1099
00:43:05,833 --> 00:43:07,750
Only Dust-Ali Khan is asleep in that room.

1100
00:43:08,208 --> 00:43:10,666
Then I'll go see how he's doing.

1101
00:43:21,000 --> 00:43:23,000
♪ music ♪

1102
00:44:10,041 --> 00:44:10,750
Leili!

1103
00:44:12,875 --> 00:44:13,416
Leili!

1104
00:44:23,166 --> 00:44:25,166
(Leili cries)

1105
00:44:33,791 --> 00:44:34,166
Leili...

1106
00:44:34,500 --> 00:44:35,791
I know you're very upset.

1107
00:44:36,416 --> 00:44:37,958
I didn't sleep all night either.

1108
00:44:38,250 --> 00:44:39,541
The whole time I was thinking of you.

1109
00:44:40,208 --> 00:44:41,875
Tomorrow Puri comes from Ahvaz.

1110
00:44:43,125 --> 00:44:44,250
Colonel Uncle said,

1111
00:44:44,291 --> 00:44:46,291
Puri telegraphed, he comes by train tomorrow.

1112
00:44:46,708 --> 00:44:47,500
I'm very afraid!

1113
00:44:47,541 --> 00:44:48,416
I'm afraid too!

1114
00:44:48,416 --> 00:44:50,458
Last night Father talked with me for an hour.

1115
00:44:51,083 --> 00:44:53,500
If they force me, I'll do away with myself.

1116
00:44:53,541 --> 00:44:54,458
No, Leili, no!

1117
00:44:59,958 --> 00:45:02,583
Hey, Leili! Where are you?

1118
00:45:04,583 --> 00:45:05,958
Saeed! Hide, so he doesn't see you!

1119
00:45:06,333 --> 00:45:07,166
Coming!

1120
00:45:19,583 --> 00:45:21,125
What's eating you, moping like that?

1121
00:45:21,166 --> 00:45:21,666
Hello!

1122
00:45:22,250 --> 00:45:23,250
Don't worry!

1123
00:45:23,416 --> 00:45:24,208
I fixed it!

1124
00:45:24,750 --> 00:45:26,958
Long live Uncle Asdollah! What trick did you use?

1125
00:45:27,125 --> 00:45:29,208
I went to the head of the criminal-affairs branch.

1126
00:45:29,625 --> 00:45:30,250
He was a good man.

1127
00:45:30,291 --> 00:45:30,916
I'd met him a few times in the old days,

1128
00:45:30,958 --> 00:45:32,291
at the house of Aziz-os-Saltaneh's late husband,

1129
00:45:32,333 --> 00:45:33,750
Qamar's father.

1130
00:45:34,291 --> 00:45:36,250
I explained that it was a family dispute.

1131
00:45:36,666 --> 00:45:38,541
We agreed that when your Dear Uncle goes to him,

1132
00:45:38,708 --> 00:45:40,375
he'll somehow walk back what he said.

1133
00:45:41,375 --> 00:45:43,083
He himself had told Lady Aziz-os-Saltaneh

1134
00:45:43,083 --> 00:45:44,666
that the unknown caller

1135
00:45:44,708 --> 00:45:45,708
had a husky voice!

1136
00:45:45,791 --> 00:45:47,625
He can't go back on his own word now

1137
00:45:47,666 --> 00:45:49,625
and say the caller sounded like a woman! -Moment!

1138
00:45:49,666 --> 00:45:50,458
Moment!

1139
00:45:50,916 --> 00:45:52,750
Who said he has to say it sounded like a woman?

1140
00:45:53,333 --> 00:45:54,541
We sat and talked for a good while,

1141
00:45:54,583 --> 00:45:55,708
we found a way out!

1142
00:45:56,083 --> 00:45:57,166
At last he remembered

1143
00:45:57,208 --> 00:45:58,625
that on the telephone he told Lady Aziz-os-Saltaneh

1144
00:45:58,666 --> 00:46:00,541
an unknown person telephoned him!

1145
00:46:00,583 --> 00:46:02,375
He never said whether it was a woman or a man!

1146
00:46:02,875 --> 00:46:04,208
Now he'll tell your Dear Uncle

1147
00:46:04,208 --> 00:46:06,125
a lady with a husky voice called him!

1148
00:46:06,500 --> 00:46:08,125
A lady with a husky voice?!

1149
00:46:08,541 --> 00:46:09,458
Who can it be?

1150
00:46:09,625 --> 00:46:11,208
Dear Uncle won't believe it at all!

1151
00:46:11,500 --> 00:46:13,250
What if it is Lady Farrokh-Laqa?!

1152
00:46:14,375 --> 00:46:16,791
Have you forgotten how, ever since she lost that ass Dust-Ali,

1153
00:46:16,791 --> 00:46:18,500
she's been Aziz-os-Saltaneh's enemy?

1154
00:46:19,750 --> 00:46:22,083
That black-clad, foul-mouthed jinx,

1155
00:46:22,083 --> 00:46:23,708
with that slack, mannish voice of hers!

1156
00:46:24,458 --> 00:46:26,125
Long live Uncle Asdollah!

1157
00:46:26,250 --> 00:46:27,250
That was smart thinking!

1158
00:46:27,333 --> 00:46:28,291
If you weren't there,

1159
00:46:28,333 --> 00:46:30,208
a war would start between Agha Joon and Dear Uncle,

1160
00:46:30,333 --> 00:46:32,125
a hundred times worse than the last one!

1161
00:46:32,791 --> 00:46:33,583
What's up, you rascal!

1162
00:46:33,625 --> 00:46:35,125
What were you saying in Leili's ear? Huh?

1163
00:46:36,375 --> 00:46:37,916
Colonel Uncle had told Leili

1164
00:46:37,958 --> 00:46:39,958
Puri comes from Ahvaz by train tomorrow!

1165
00:46:39,958 --> 00:46:40,541
Well, well!

1166
00:46:40,583 --> 00:46:42,291
I suppose you're planning to go to the station

1167
00:46:42,333 --> 00:46:43,375
to meet him!

1168
00:46:43,541 --> 00:46:44,916
To welcome him, right?!

1169
00:46:45,458 --> 00:46:45,958
Uncle Asdollah!

1170
00:46:46,000 --> 00:46:47,416
You're always teasing me!

1171
00:46:47,458 --> 00:46:48,375
How is it my fault?!

1172
00:46:48,416 --> 00:46:49,666
Every time, between Agha Joon and Dear Uncle,

1173
00:46:49,708 --> 00:46:50,666
a war breaks out,

1174
00:46:50,666 --> 00:46:52,666
first of all they separate me and Leili!

1175
00:46:53,125 --> 00:46:54,291
You want to know why?

1176
00:46:54,458 --> 00:46:55,458
Well, it's obvious!

1177
00:46:55,500 --> 00:46:56,416
Because you deserve it!

1178
00:47:00,625 --> 00:47:02,208
My boy, I'm blue in the face!

1179
00:47:02,250 --> 00:47:02,958
I've told you a hundred times,

1180
00:47:03,000 --> 00:47:04,291
take Leili and go on a trip,

1181
00:47:04,291 --> 00:47:05,541
San Fran-cisco!

1182
00:47:05,791 --> 00:47:07,333
I can't! But how?!

1183
00:47:09,375 --> 00:47:09,833
Go!

1184
00:47:09,958 --> 00:47:10,666
Don't be afraid!

1185
00:47:11,208 --> 00:47:12,875
Put your mind at ease, and mine, and everyone's!

1186
00:47:18,333 --> 00:47:19,041
Why don't you come in?

1187
00:47:19,250 --> 00:47:20,125
Are you sulking?

1188
00:47:20,333 --> 00:47:21,125
No, Uncle Asdollah!

1189
00:47:21,166 --> 00:47:23,166
Whenever Agha Joon and Dear Uncle fall out,

1190
00:47:23,166 --> 00:47:25,041
Dear Uncle gets angry as soon as he sees me!

1191
00:47:25,833 --> 00:47:27,458
Then stay nearby until I call you!

1192
00:47:35,166 --> 00:47:37,166
♪ traditional music ♪

1193
00:47:50,000 --> 00:47:51,125
Please, Sir!

1194
00:47:51,208 --> 00:47:52,000
Hello, Dear Uncle!

1195
00:47:52,916 --> 00:47:54,666
Hello, son! How are you, Saeed dear?-

1196
00:47:54,916 --> 00:47:56,500
All alone?!

1197
00:47:56,750 --> 00:47:58,208
Where are the children?

1198
00:47:58,750 --> 00:48:00,166
Akh akh akh akh...-

1199
00:48:00,166 --> 00:48:01,625
Is your father home?

1200
00:48:01,958 --> 00:48:03,333
Yes, Dear Uncle. Do you need him?

1201
00:48:03,541 --> 00:48:05,416
I'll come see him myself.

1202
00:48:05,583 --> 00:48:08,458
Let me first go change my clothes.

1203
00:48:08,458 --> 00:48:09,333
Then I'll come. At your service, Dear Uncle-

1204
00:48:09,375 --> 00:48:09,958
Then I'll tell him.

1205
00:48:10,250 --> 00:48:12,250
♪ piano music ♪

1206
00:49:16,791 --> 00:49:17,708
Oh!

1207
00:49:20,583 --> 00:49:23,041
Salaam alaykom, Sir! Welcome back!

1208
00:49:23,166 --> 00:49:25,833
Ghasem! Give me a glass of that drinking water!

1209
00:49:25,875 --> 00:49:26,708
At your service, Sir!

1210
00:49:28,583 --> 00:49:29,333
Please!

1211
00:49:30,041 --> 00:49:32,333
Looks like the heat's got to you. It's very hot today!-

1212
00:49:36,791 --> 00:49:38,458
Naneh Zivar won't agree to it!

1213
00:49:38,500 --> 00:49:40,833
She says she's too far along! It can't be aborted!

1214
00:49:41,375 --> 00:49:42,958
Is there a better midwife than Naneh Zivar

1215
00:49:43,000 --> 00:49:44,250
in this city?

1216
00:49:44,625 --> 00:49:45,916
Even she can't do anything now!

1217
00:49:45,916 --> 00:49:47,208
Now that there's no remedy,

1218
00:49:47,250 --> 00:49:49,333
we must find someone, somehow,

1219
00:49:49,375 --> 00:49:50,875
who, even if only for a few days,

1220
00:49:50,916 --> 00:49:51,916
will marry Qamar!

1221
00:49:52,750 --> 00:49:55,583
There's Mamad Sir the electrician down the alley!

1222
00:49:55,583 --> 00:49:56,041
Well?!

1223
00:49:56,083 --> 00:49:57,416
I think he doesn't have a wife!

1224
00:49:57,416 --> 00:49:57,958
He's a bachelor!

1225
00:49:58,208 --> 00:49:58,708
Hello, Sir!

1226
00:49:58,750 --> 00:49:59,791
He weds Qamar for a few days, Hello, Shazdeh-

1227
00:49:59,833 --> 00:50:01,125
and after that he divorces her, that's all!

1228
00:50:01,166 --> 00:50:01,708
Uh-huh!

1229
00:50:01,875 --> 00:50:04,125
Aren't you ashamed, Dust-Ali?

1230
00:50:04,375 --> 00:50:07,291
Mamad Sir the electrician, our son-in-law?!

1231
00:50:07,583 --> 00:50:10,208
Who can bear this shame?!

1232
00:50:10,791 --> 00:50:12,666
A noble family, Yes, Sir!!-

1233
00:50:12,666 --> 00:50:14,708
marrying into an electrician's?! Yes!-

1234
00:50:14,833 --> 00:50:16,208
with a nobody?

1235
00:50:16,625 --> 00:50:18,250
God take me!

1236
00:50:18,458 --> 00:50:21,083
What hopes I had for this poor girl!

1237
00:50:21,208 --> 00:50:22,291
Now my child

1238
00:50:22,333 --> 00:50:23,833
has to marry Mamad Sir the electrician!

1239
00:50:24,041 --> 00:50:24,791
Mamad Sir!

1240
00:50:24,916 --> 00:50:26,416
Don't even think of it!

1241
00:50:26,791 --> 00:50:27,375
Why?!

1242
00:50:28,250 --> 00:50:29,916
Mamad Sir has an illness!

1243
00:50:30,458 --> 00:50:31,375
What illness?

1244
00:50:31,791 --> 00:50:34,166
Pardon my saying so, in front of the lady!

1245
00:50:34,250 --> 00:50:35,916
Mamad Sir is not a man at all!

1246
00:50:37,458 --> 00:50:38,500
How do you know!

1247
00:50:38,541 --> 00:50:39,416
To hell!

1248
00:50:39,625 --> 00:50:41,958
Damn him, man or no man!

1249
00:50:42,208 --> 00:50:43,958
Don't even mention him!

1250
00:50:44,375 --> 00:50:47,041
Sir! It doesn't hurt to ask, my dear!

1251
00:50:47,583 --> 00:50:49,708
We may have no choice in the end!

1252
00:50:49,916 --> 00:50:51,083
Well, Mash Ghasem, say,

1253
00:50:51,333 --> 00:50:53,625
how do you know Dust-Ali isn't a man?!

1254
00:50:53,916 --> 00:50:55,583
You mean... Mamad Sir is not a man?!

1255
00:50:55,583 --> 00:50:56,041
Yes!

1256
00:50:56,208 --> 00:50:57,291
Why lie, Sir?

1257
00:50:57,375 --> 00:50:59,083
The grave is this close!

1258
00:50:59,375 --> 00:51:01,458
We didn't see anything with our own eyes!

1259
00:51:01,916 --> 00:51:03,916
We heard it from Ebrahim Sir the grocer!

1260
00:51:04,250 --> 00:51:06,083
And he heard it from the baker's wife!

1261
00:51:06,291 --> 00:51:08,541
Agha Reza, that haberdasher,

1262
00:51:08,666 --> 00:51:10,291
had told the baker's wife!

1263
00:51:10,541 --> 00:51:13,250
Agha Reza himself said he heard it from Shir-Ali's wife!

1264
00:51:13,583 --> 00:51:15,500
Shir-Ali's wife heard it from someone else too,

1265
00:51:15,500 --> 00:51:17,208
who God knows... I mean...

1266
00:51:17,416 --> 00:51:19,041
I mean, she heard it from a person

1267
00:51:19,041 --> 00:51:20,750
whose name we cannot say, Sir!

1268
00:51:20,791 --> 00:51:21,708
You've named everyone!

1269
00:51:21,750 --> 00:51:22,791
Go on, name this one too!

1270
00:51:22,833 --> 00:51:24,166
No, Sir! We cannot say!

1271
00:51:24,416 --> 00:51:26,958
Tear us limb from limb, we cannot say!

1272
00:51:27,625 --> 00:51:29,416
Your own family is involved!

1273
00:51:29,458 --> 00:51:30,458
Moment!

1274
00:51:30,500 --> 00:51:32,458
Man or not, it doesn't matter!

1275
00:51:32,458 --> 00:51:33,208
Does it?

1276
00:51:33,750 --> 00:51:35,625
After all, the job he'd have to do,

1277
00:51:35,666 --> 00:51:37,125
someone already did!

1278
00:51:37,125 --> 00:51:37,708
Yes? Yes!-

1279
00:51:38,375 --> 00:51:39,125
Obviously!

1280
00:51:39,416 --> 00:51:41,416
I know someone who'd die for this job!

1281
00:51:41,458 --> 00:51:42,041
Shut up!

1282
00:51:43,083 --> 00:51:43,791
Hey, Dust-Ali!

1283
00:51:44,125 --> 00:51:44,583
Sir!

1284
00:51:44,583 --> 00:51:45,625
I didn't mean you!

1285
00:51:45,625 --> 00:51:47,583
We know someone else,

1286
00:51:47,583 --> 00:51:48,666
if he's willing,

1287
00:51:48,833 --> 00:51:51,208
a man of standing and accomplishments!

1288
00:51:51,708 --> 00:51:53,541
He's from our own Ghiyasabad!

1289
00:51:53,583 --> 00:51:54,791
He has no illness either!

1290
00:51:54,833 --> 00:51:56,375
We'll vouch for him ourselves!

1291
00:51:56,833 --> 00:51:57,333
Who?

1292
00:51:58,291 --> 00:52:00,875
Remember that Ghiyasabadi who one day

1293
00:52:00,875 --> 00:52:03,166
had come along with that Nayeb Teymour Khan,

1294
00:52:03,291 --> 00:52:04,583
God forbid,

1295
00:52:04,625 --> 00:52:07,000
came looking for Mr. Dust-Ali Khan's corpse?

1296
00:52:07,041 --> 00:52:07,958
What was his name?

1297
00:52:08,333 --> 00:52:09,583
Ah! The Ghiyasabadi aspiran!

1298
00:52:09,625 --> 00:52:11,541
Ah! Yes, Sir, yes!

1299
00:52:11,625 --> 00:52:13,375
It seems like just yesterday!

1300
00:52:14,166 --> 00:52:15,541
We recall,

1301
00:52:15,625 --> 00:52:17,250
that day they had come,

1302
00:52:17,291 --> 00:52:18,916
when they saw Lady Qamar,

1303
00:52:19,083 --> 00:52:21,875
they were drooling all over themselves!

1304
00:52:21,875 --> 00:52:24,000
Ghiyasabadis like their women plump!

1305
00:52:24,041 --> 00:52:26,291
Asdollah! Is this the time for such talk!

1306
00:52:26,458 --> 00:52:28,041
Shut up, Ghasem!

1307
00:52:28,500 --> 00:52:31,000
The Ghiyasabadi aspiran, our son-in-law?

1308
00:52:31,083 --> 00:52:32,708
Have some shame and decency!

1309
00:52:32,958 --> 00:52:34,041
It's shameful!

1310
00:52:34,208 --> 00:52:35,375
Sir, allow us

1311
00:52:35,375 --> 00:52:37,666
to see if this Ghiyasabadi fellow is even a man!

1312
00:52:37,666 --> 00:52:38,750
Why lie, Sir?

1313
00:52:38,833 --> 00:52:40,541
The grave is this close!

1314
00:52:40,708 --> 00:52:42,541
We didn't see it with our own eyes!

1315
00:52:42,583 --> 00:52:45,208
But Qom's Ghiyasabad has no unmanly men!

1316
00:52:45,583 --> 00:52:47,416
As for the other Ghiyasabad, we can't say!

1317
00:52:47,458 --> 00:52:49,541
All the women of Qom and Kashan and Isfahan,

1318
00:52:49,583 --> 00:52:50,750
with some of Tehran's women,

1319
00:52:50,916 --> 00:52:52,833
die for Qom's Ghiyasabadis!

1320
00:52:53,500 --> 00:52:56,208
Show some shame before me!

1321
00:52:56,375 --> 00:52:58,000
We had a fellow townsman...

1322
00:52:58,041 --> 00:52:59,375
You shut up already, Ghasem!

1323
00:52:59,958 --> 00:53:01,625
Shamelessness has its limits!

1324
00:53:01,666 --> 00:53:02,791
Moment! Moment!

1325
00:53:02,833 --> 00:53:04,875
Sir, what shamelessness!

1326
00:53:05,416 --> 00:53:07,708
An innocent, simple-minded girl

1327
00:53:07,958 --> 00:53:09,541
has landed in trouble!

1328
00:53:10,000 --> 00:53:12,375
Either Allahverdi, the Indian Sardar's servant,

1329
00:53:12,833 --> 00:53:15,166
or some other shameless good-for-nothing,

1330
00:53:15,166 --> 00:53:16,625
has done this to her and,

1331
00:53:16,958 --> 00:53:18,541
now he's playing dumb!

1332
00:53:19,333 --> 00:53:21,958
An abortion could kill her!

1333
00:53:22,416 --> 00:53:23,791
Only one way remains!

1334
00:53:23,916 --> 00:53:25,333
To find her a husband!

1335
00:53:25,666 --> 00:53:27,875
And even that is for your reputation's sake!

1336
00:53:28,125 --> 00:53:30,000
Honestly, she isn't upset at all!

1337
00:53:30,416 --> 00:53:32,166
She's ready to have the baby without a husband,

1338
00:53:32,208 --> 00:53:33,583
and raise it!

1339
00:53:33,958 --> 00:53:35,416
Now you expect

1340
00:53:35,500 --> 00:53:37,833
Palang-os-Saltaneh's son, or Babr-od-Dowleh's grandson,

1341
00:53:37,833 --> 00:53:38,875
to come ask for her hand?!

1342
00:53:39,125 --> 00:53:41,875
Stop already, Shazdeh!

1343
00:53:41,958 --> 00:53:43,875
You must know

1344
00:53:43,958 --> 00:53:48,666
what an aristocratic family's honor and reputation mean!

1345
00:53:48,958 --> 00:53:50,916
Many may not know!

1346
00:53:50,958 --> 00:53:53,375
But you must know!

1347
00:53:53,375 --> 00:53:55,166
I know... I know...

1348
00:53:55,250 --> 00:53:56,166
Meaning,

1349
00:53:56,583 --> 00:53:59,500
the daughter of Lord So-and-so and granddaughter of Duke Such-and-such

1350
00:53:59,833 --> 00:54:01,541
must not become a Ghiyasabadi's wife!

1351
00:54:02,041 --> 00:54:04,666
If you know George VI, which you surely do,

1352
00:54:04,666 --> 00:54:06,250
tell me, and I'll send him a telegram

1353
00:54:06,291 --> 00:54:08,541
to send the wedding mirror and candlesticks!

1354
00:54:17,625 --> 00:54:19,708
Maybe the Shazdeh is right too!

1355
00:54:20,500 --> 00:54:22,791
It's not my place to interfere at all!

1356
00:54:24,250 --> 00:54:26,875
Yes! That's her mother, and that's her stepfather!

1357
00:54:27,125 --> 00:54:29,000
Let them decide for her themselves!

1358
00:54:29,208 --> 00:54:33,458
And her stepfather is such a caring, respectable man!

1359
00:54:34,166 --> 00:54:35,208
He's just lying there!

1360
00:54:35,250 --> 00:54:35,833
Acting as if

1361
00:54:35,833 --> 00:54:37,583
he weren't the one who caused this mess!

1362
00:54:38,250 --> 00:54:40,708
Get up and do something, you lazy lump!

1363
00:54:41,166 --> 00:54:42,625
May you sleep forever!

1364
00:54:42,666 --> 00:54:43,250
Enough!

1365
00:54:43,250 --> 00:54:44,625
Stop talking such drivel, Asdollah!

1366
00:54:44,666 --> 00:54:45,833
On my father's soul, if...

1367
00:54:45,833 --> 00:54:46,291
Shut up!

1368
00:54:47,250 --> 00:54:47,958
Shut your trap!

1369
00:54:48,250 --> 00:54:49,291
Vile, stinking wretch!

1370
00:54:50,125 --> 00:54:52,041
Shazdeh! Please!

1371
00:54:52,333 --> 00:54:55,583
Now I have no doubt left

1372
00:54:55,625 --> 00:54:57,833
that this matter is a plot!

1373
00:54:57,958 --> 00:55:00,791
The plot of those who want to destroy me!

1374
00:55:01,041 --> 00:55:03,833
This plot has been dictated from London!

1375
00:55:04,166 --> 00:55:07,708
That good-for-nothing Indian spy drew up the plan,

1376
00:55:07,833 --> 00:55:10,833
and his shameless servant carried it out!

1377
00:55:12,458 --> 00:55:15,083
So in your view, whoever the English have it in for,

1378
00:55:15,291 --> 00:55:16,708
they assign some brute

1379
00:55:16,708 --> 00:55:18,333
to dishonor his uncle's granddaughter, huh?

1380
00:55:18,416 --> 00:55:20,458
Don't say nonsense!

1381
00:55:20,708 --> 00:55:22,625
Don't twist things!

1382
00:55:22,833 --> 00:55:24,250
It'll be a long time yet

1383
00:55:24,291 --> 00:55:27,541
before you figure out this old wolf's tricks!

1384
00:55:27,708 --> 00:55:30,166
And to think you work at the Foreign Ministry!

1385
00:55:30,458 --> 00:55:31,291
So by that logic,

1386
00:55:31,291 --> 00:55:33,958
Hitler's uncle's granddaughter and Mussolini's uncle's granddaughter,

1387
00:55:34,000 --> 00:55:35,958
must each have had three babies by now!

1388
00:55:36,291 --> 00:55:36,833
Asdollah!

1389
00:55:36,875 --> 00:55:38,125
Am I lying?!

1390
00:55:38,541 --> 00:55:39,458
Ugh!

1391
00:55:39,500 --> 00:55:40,375
Madam dear!

1392
00:55:40,500 --> 00:55:42,583
I've decided to propose Sir's method

1393
00:55:42,625 --> 00:55:44,166
to Churchill!

1394
00:55:44,458 --> 00:55:45,833
From now on, the English gentlemen

1395
00:55:45,875 --> 00:55:48,291
must close their arms-making factories,

1396
00:55:48,375 --> 00:55:50,083
and make potency pills!

1397
00:55:50,166 --> 00:55:52,208
Personally, I'm truly sorry that

1398
00:55:52,250 --> 00:55:55,333
I'm not in the English Foreign Ministry's army of avengers!

1399
00:55:56,666 --> 00:55:58,208
How do we know you're not?

1400
00:55:58,208 --> 00:55:59,916
On your grave, I'm not!

1401
00:56:00,000 --> 00:56:01,541
If I were, instead of raisins,

1402
00:56:01,583 --> 00:56:03,166
I'd be popping potency pills!

1403
00:56:03,208 --> 00:56:04,416
Calm down, Sir!

1404
00:56:04,416 --> 00:56:06,541
Who says our fellow townsman will even accept!

1405
00:56:06,625 --> 00:56:08,791
To hell with you and every Ghiyasabadi there is! Why? Why, Sir! Eh!-

1406
00:56:09,125 --> 00:56:10,583
Well, you were saying about the Ghiyasabadi!

1407
00:56:10,625 --> 00:56:11,458
Why lie, Sir?

1408
00:56:11,500 --> 00:56:13,083
The grave is this close!

1409
00:56:13,708 --> 00:56:14,791
True, our fellow townsman

1410
00:56:14,791 --> 00:56:16,708
really has his eye on Qamar Khanom,

1411
00:56:17,166 --> 00:56:18,875
but when it comes to family honor,

1412
00:56:18,916 --> 00:56:20,875
put all of Iran on one side,

1413
00:56:21,000 --> 00:56:24,250
and Ghiyasabad on the other!

1414
00:56:24,750 --> 00:56:27,000
We had a fellow townsman... Stop your yapping!-

1415
00:56:27,291 --> 00:56:29,000
To hell with you and your fellow townsmen!

1416
00:56:29,166 --> 00:56:30,666
You had a fellow townsman again?!

1417
00:56:31,166 --> 00:56:32,666
Let him have his say!

1418
00:56:32,791 --> 00:56:34,416
Don't you want to be free of this mess

1419
00:56:34,416 --> 00:56:35,375
you've made?

1420
00:56:36,208 --> 00:56:37,208
Go on, Mash Ghasem!

1421
00:56:39,000 --> 00:56:39,666
At your service!

1422
00:56:40,000 --> 00:56:40,833
Yes, Sir!

1423
00:56:40,958 --> 00:56:42,416
We had a fellow townsman

1424
00:56:42,458 --> 00:56:44,041
who had married off two sons.

1425
00:56:45,416 --> 00:56:46,625
Then one day he heard

1426
00:56:46,625 --> 00:56:48,500
that before their wedding, at the shrine,

1427
00:56:48,708 --> 00:56:50,500
his wife's chador had slipped off!

1428
00:56:50,541 --> 00:56:51,458
He divorced his wife!

1429
00:56:52,916 --> 00:56:55,041
Even so, all the Ghiyasabadis taunted him

1430
00:56:55,083 --> 00:56:56,625
for not cutting off his wife's head!

1431
00:56:57,875 --> 00:57:00,708
From then on, he was known as dishonorable!

1432
00:57:01,416 --> 00:57:04,166
Three days later, he died of shame!

1433
00:57:06,125 --> 00:57:08,208
I'm telling you this so you don't think

1434
00:57:08,208 --> 00:57:09,250
you can

1435
00:57:09,291 --> 00:57:11,291
saddle our fellow townsman with Lady Qamar!

1436
00:57:12,000 --> 00:57:15,125
No need to tell him about Qamar's pregnancy!

1437
00:57:15,250 --> 00:57:16,291
Why would we?

1438
00:57:17,041 --> 00:57:19,125
You think Ghiyasabadis are such donkeys?!

1439
00:57:19,833 --> 00:57:21,625
We had another fellow townsman

1440
00:57:21,666 --> 00:57:24,541
who went to ask for a girl's hand... -Moment!

1441
00:57:24,541 --> 00:57:27,125
Moment, Mash Ghasem!

1442
00:57:27,583 --> 00:57:29,166
If no one says anything,

1443
00:57:29,208 --> 00:57:31,083
how will this fellow townsman of yours find out?

1444
00:57:31,791 --> 00:57:32,208
But!

1445
00:57:32,541 --> 00:57:33,708
Why lie, Sir?

1446
00:57:33,708 --> 00:57:35,583
The grave is this close!

1447
00:57:36,583 --> 00:57:38,958
No offense, we don't know about Tehran folk!

1448
00:57:39,750 --> 00:57:40,791
But in Ghiyasabad,

1449
00:57:40,833 --> 00:57:42,958
women and girls are different!

1450
00:57:43,958 --> 00:57:44,916
Merci, Mash Ghasem!

1451
00:57:44,958 --> 00:57:46,750
Thanks for the information!

1452
00:57:46,791 --> 00:57:47,708
If I'm not mistaken,

1453
00:57:47,708 --> 00:57:49,500
you mean the women of Ghiyasabad

1454
00:57:49,541 --> 00:57:51,208
have been to San Francisco,

1455
00:57:51,541 --> 00:57:53,250
but their daughters haven't!

1456
00:57:53,291 --> 00:57:53,916
Bravo!

1457
00:57:54,125 --> 00:57:55,625
That's what we meant!

1458
00:57:56,000 --> 00:57:58,458
Mr. Aspiran may not understand at first!

1459
00:57:58,625 --> 00:58:00,166
But because he's a Ghiyasabadi,

1460
00:58:00,208 --> 00:58:01,541
he'll surely find out on the wedding night!

1461
00:58:01,583 --> 00:58:02,375
Moment!

1462
00:58:02,458 --> 00:58:06,250
But given how protective of honor Ghiyasabadis are,

1463
00:58:06,541 --> 00:58:08,083
I don't think Mr. Aspiran

1464
00:58:08,125 --> 00:58:09,125
will go up on the roof

1465
00:58:09,125 --> 00:58:10,333
and shout!

1466
00:58:11,000 --> 00:58:12,041
I think,

1467
00:58:12,333 --> 00:58:13,541
even if he understands,

1468
00:58:13,666 --> 00:58:15,208
at most he'll divorce her!

1469
00:58:15,208 --> 00:58:15,625
Yes!

1470
00:58:15,625 --> 00:58:17,208
Isn't that exactly what you want?!

1471
00:58:17,500 --> 00:58:19,416
Someone marries Qamar,

1472
00:58:19,541 --> 00:58:21,333
and a few days later divorces her!

1473
00:58:21,708 --> 00:58:22,791
This is dishonorable!

1474
00:58:22,833 --> 00:58:23,583
It's unconscionable!

1475
00:58:23,625 --> 00:58:24,750
He must be told about the baby

1476
00:58:24,791 --> 00:58:26,458
openly, right from the start!

1477
00:58:29,875 --> 00:58:31,458
You have to pick one!

1478
00:58:31,583 --> 00:58:33,333
Son-in-law or conscience!

1479
00:58:33,333 --> 00:58:34,500
Let's take a vote!

1480
00:58:35,041 --> 00:58:37,583
I vote for the son-in-law!

1481
00:58:38,083 --> 00:58:40,916
And you, Dust-Ali, Lord of Conscience,

1482
00:58:41,083 --> 00:58:42,583
vote for conscience!

1483
00:58:43,000 --> 00:58:44,916
In defense of my position, I say

1484
00:58:44,958 --> 00:58:48,125
that nothing unconscionable is being done!

1485
00:58:48,625 --> 00:58:50,000
The Ghiyasabadi aspiran

1486
00:58:50,166 --> 00:58:52,458
eats and sleeps free for a few days.

1487
00:58:52,750 --> 00:58:54,708
He becomes Lady Aziz-os-Saltaneh's son-in-law.

1488
00:58:55,125 --> 00:58:57,083
And it costs him nothing,

1489
00:58:57,833 --> 00:59:00,416
plus a free trip to San Francisco!

1490
00:59:00,416 --> 00:59:02,333
I'd move to Ghiyasabad for that!

1491
00:59:02,541 --> 00:59:04,041
God willing, God will grant

1492
00:59:04,041 --> 00:59:05,958
you and me such luck too!

1493
00:59:07,541 --> 00:59:08,666
You were conceived

1494
00:59:08,791 --> 00:59:10,500
in liquor and wine!

1495
00:59:10,500 --> 00:59:11,958
Moment!

1496
00:59:12,083 --> 00:59:15,291
And you, conceived in holy water and rosewater,

1497
00:59:15,375 --> 00:59:19,416
you'd hate to have them pay your way, beg you to accept,

1498
00:59:20,041 --> 00:59:22,291
give you free lunch and dinner,

1499
00:59:22,708 --> 00:59:25,375
and with a plump young companion

1500
00:59:25,708 --> 00:59:28,166
send you to San Francisco for a few days, yes?

1501
00:59:28,458 --> 00:59:30,083
If it stings, say 'ouch'!

1502
00:59:30,375 --> 00:59:31,916
What is this nonsense you're saying?

1503
00:59:31,916 --> 00:59:33,375
To hell with both your ugly faces!

1504
00:59:33,500 --> 00:59:35,125
Has my daughter sunk so low

1505
00:59:35,166 --> 00:59:36,708
that you have to beg that Ghiyasabadi?!

1506
00:59:36,833 --> 00:59:38,708
Was my daughter born in a ditch?

1507
00:59:39,833 --> 00:59:41,541
Don't get angry, Madam!

1508
00:59:41,750 --> 00:59:43,291
Granted, Lady Qamar

1509
00:59:43,333 --> 00:59:44,666
wasn't born in a ditch!

1510
00:59:44,875 --> 00:59:46,666
Maybe the aspiran won't want a wife!

1511
00:59:46,708 --> 00:59:47,833
And even if he does,

1512
00:59:47,875 --> 00:59:49,833
maybe Qamar won't want him!

1513
00:59:49,875 --> 00:59:51,083
Qamar wouldn't dare!

1514
00:59:51,208 --> 00:59:52,000
Then, Lady Aziz!

1515
00:59:52,041 --> 00:59:53,708
Go talk with Qamar,

1516
00:59:53,750 --> 00:59:54,666
and if she agrees,

1517
00:59:54,666 --> 00:59:56,625
I'll send Mash Ghasem to the aspiran,

1518
00:59:56,708 --> 00:59:58,208
before it's too late!

1519
00:59:58,500 --> 00:59:59,083
But...

1520
00:59:59,750 --> 01:00:01,500
But this poor girl of mine

1521
01:00:01,500 --> 01:00:02,958
understands nothing.

1522
01:00:04,541 --> 01:00:05,958
Whenever I ask her something,

1523
01:00:06,000 --> 01:00:07,791
she just answers with nonsense.

1524
01:00:07,791 --> 01:00:09,250
Allow me to go talk with her.

1525
01:00:09,250 --> 01:00:09,750
Hmm?

1526
01:00:09,750 --> 01:00:11,250
You won't get anything out of her either.

1527
01:00:11,291 --> 01:00:12,791
God take me.

1528
01:00:12,833 --> 01:00:14,583
Since this disaster struck her,

1529
01:00:14,666 --> 01:00:16,125
she's lost her mind!

1530
01:00:16,375 --> 01:00:17,708
I'll go and talk her into it.

1531
01:00:19,875 --> 01:00:21,875
♪ Ride of the valkyrie ♪

